{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future","id":363273,"title":"What kind of books would you like in the future?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-08T01:09:58-08:00","id":363273,"title":"What kind of books would you like in the future?","content":"Hi guys,<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if that kind of thread already exist, but i didn\u2019t find one. The idea is to collect your wishes for futures projects for the cWoD collection and, why not, submit it to the OPP team.<br /> <br /> Here are my personal whishes:<br /> <br /> - V20:<ul><li>Guide to the Unknown (First ed was a really disappointment)</li> <li>Book of Antiquity: I don\u2019t know what should be the form, just a sourcebook or a stand-alone as DA, but I would really loved to have some details Of Rome, Sparte, Carthage and stuff like that. Background, new rules and that kind of things. It would make a great KS too.</li> <li>Guide to the laibon</li> </ul>- W20:<ul><li>Tribebook Bunyip</li> <li>A campaign focused on Umbra. I always had trouble to create a specific campaign on that theme.</li> </ul>- M20:<br /> I never really play this game, so I\u2019m just following the movement without really new idea on it.<br /> <br /> - Wr 20:<ul><li>A book focused on the American civil war would be interesting!</li> </ul>- C20:<ul><li>A core rulebook? ;-)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> And you ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3879-black-lion","name":"Black Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T03:43:35-08:00","id":363313,"title":"","content":"Aside what is already announced/planned to come out for W20, V20, my which list is really small:<br /> <br /> W20<ul><li>Tribebook: Croatan (I'm aware that Croatan song also acts as their clanbook, but still).</li> <li>Tribebook: Bunyip</li> <li>DA: Mummy (or a Mummy sourcebook for DA)</li> <li>DA: Wraith (or a Wraith sourcebook for DA)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":".  Added the 2 DA product to my list 01-21-2015, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T03:59:36-08:00","id":363327,"title":"","content":"My Wishlist goes something like this.<br /> <br /> M20<ul><li>M20 Traditions Gathered + Guide to the Traditions</li> <li>M20 Conventions Gathered + Guide to the Conventions.</li> <li>M20 Digital Web ?.0 + Infinite Tapestry + Horizon</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> C20<ul><li>The lost Book of Glamour and Kithbook Boggan</li> <li>New setting books for All the kingdoms. Pacifica, Apples, Willows, Northern Ice, ALL of them.</li> <li>A mini-book like the Silver Record, or the Book of Nod, a little leatherette piece for Changelings on Fae History. (Ahem, all in Shakespearean pentameter)</li> <li>Revised Books of Houses maybe all in one Volume</li> <li>Expanded Kithbooks all around. Maybe also all in one Volume. Maybe rules for making/ Adapting new Kith</li> <li>New and expanded rules for the Dreaming and what goes on there.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T10:58:19-08:00","id":363681,"title":"","content":"For Changeling 20, I hope we'll get a great corebook with all the arts, realms and Kithain kiths + Gallain info in the same way Changing Breeds were featured in W20 and them we could have a Book of Gallain with all the expended info for Nunnehi, Inanimae, Menehune, Thallain, Hsien, Adhene...<br /> After that, I hope we finally could have Keys to the Kingdom with info about places that Changeling never talked about (South America, Egypt, Near East...).<br /> A book about other Kingdoms would be great. And one book about the Dreaming much bigger than Dreams and Nightmares.<br /> And a book about Fomorians would be fantastic!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/n6g3njp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/kpa5GS5Mp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/93820aaad7.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/584-eliseo-ap-liam","name":"Eliseo ap Liam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T12:32:40-08:00","id":363734,"title":"","content":"HtR20<br /> DtF20<br /> An Aprils Fools 20 year book<br /> a 20 year Setting book for asia<br /> A World of Darkness 20 Years<br /> <br /> Los Angels: Blood, Rage, And Shattered Dreams. A setting book for Vampire, Werewolf and Mage<br /> WtO20: Viva La Revolucion (A Wraith book for South America and the Revoluciones and Dictatorships)<br /> WtO20: By Sea, Air and Land. A setting book for The Titanic, The Hiddenburg and The Midnight Express<br /> WtO20: Spook Hunters or How i learn to be A Bioexorcist: A book detailing how humans exploit Hauntings with TV shows and Reality Shows (and how to build your own GhostHunters or Ghost Facers team) and how do Wraiths handle Spooking and scaring people away from their homes.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T14:24:48-08:00","id":363796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=363734#post363734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HtR20<br /> WtO20: By Sea, Air and Land. A setting book for The Titanic, The Hiddenburg and The Midnight Express</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea. Though the Midnight Express got its own book. I think including the Amagasaki rail crash would fit in. I'm sure the driver has got plenty of unresolved issues (given the harsh training and treatment conductors are given and being over-stressed) and it would be a good chance to include some non-western stuff.<br /> <br /> V:TM<br /> -A book on the bloodlines.<br /> -Vienna, Brasila, Cape Town, Madrid or Amsterdam by Night<br /> <br /> W:TO<br /> -A book on the Heretics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T15:59:55-08:00","id":363881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=363327#post363327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Wishlist goes something like this.<br /> <br /> M20<ul><li>M20 Traditions Gathered + Guide to the Traditions</li> <li>M20 Conventions Gathered + Guide to the Conventions.</li> <li>M20 Digital Web ?.0 + Infinite Tapestry + Horizon</li> </ul><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>+1 for basically reading my mind on my wish list.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T18:53:35-08:00","id":363990,"title":"","content":"A few that I'd really like:<br /> <br /> 1.) Beckett's Jihad Diary to be done in volumes. Or even possibly as a sort of magazine, taking trips through the metaplot as the character likewise travels the world. This could even be expanded a bit to include a look at some of the other setting metaplots, too.<br /> <br /> 2.) A World of Darkness redone. A book that takes a look at the setting WoD and how it plays out all over the world, with some small hooks and tips about each.<br /> <br /> 3.) A WoD neutral Storyteller's Guide to Crossovers, and a smaller Player's Guide, focusing on tips and tricks, playstyles, and suggestions.<br /> <br /> 4.) I'd much rather see Hunter the Reckoning 20th than anything else that hasn't been officially announced yet, (Demon, Mummy, KotE, etc. . ) Not really sure if this counts, as much as I'd rather have it than any of the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T02:32:46-08:00","id":364189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future#post363273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys,<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if that kind of thread already exist, but i didn\u2019t find one. The idea is to collect your wishes for futures projects for the cWoD collection and, why not, submit it to the OPP team.<br /> <br /> Here are my personal whishes:<br /> <br /> - V20:[*]Book of Antiquity: I don\u2019t know what should be the form, just a sourcebook or a stand-alone as DA, but I would really loved to have some details Of Rome, Sparte, Carthage and stuff like that. Background, new rules and that kind of things. It would make a great KS too.[*]Guide to the laibon</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes please! A core book on Classical Antiquity would be awesome!<br /> <br /> Guide to Laibon would also be very welcome, as would a book on Cainites of the East written in the same style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T05:25:07-08:00","id":364254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=364189#post364189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes please! A core book on Classical Antiquity would be awesome!<br /> <br /> Guide to Laibon would also be very welcome, as would a book on Cainites of the East written in the same style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from the Cainites of the East, which we have see Winds from the East or whatever the books name was, these would be awesome. And of course KotE20th would be awesome as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T09:08:36-08:00","id":364457,"title":"","content":"Based on what I've seen from posts, I'm betting the Reckoning and Kindred of the East have enough of a dedicated fan-base to get 20th Ed, Kickstarter and all. The success of the Wraith20 KS and the upcoming Changeling20 show that Onyx is cool with going for the games other than the &quot;Big Three&quot;. (Though, technically, I guess KoE is a part of Vampire, so KoE20 COULD get handled as a supplement to V20, but.... they're really really different in so many ways, maybe it's time for it to put on big boy pants and go it alone...) <br /> <br /> I'm not sure about Fallen. I would like to think so, but I'm not sure. Though I have it and have read the core book, I haven't gotten a chance to try to run or play it, so I'm not really qualified to speak about it. (Though I'd certainly like to hear more from DtF partisans.)<br /> <br /> Mummy.... No. I don't think so. I like it (and did run a brief chronicle.... man those guys are powerful), but I don't like the chances for it. At all. Maybe V20 can pick that one up as well as KotE20? A sort of &quot;People that were once dead but aren't anymore, kinda like vampires, only not....&quot;<br /> <br /> I am a pessimist so I'm going to keep my wish list to things it's likely I'll get way. It minimizes the potential for future disappointment....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T12:06:52-08:00","id":364653,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, a setting book for V:TM (and to a lesser extent, the others) set in Ancient Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T13:52:12-08:00","id":364751,"title":"","content":"i was thinking on an interesting setting book<br /> <br /> World of Darkness: A Ring a Ding Ding.<br /> A setting book set in LAs Vegas and Hollywood from the years 1940 to the 1960s. involving The Mafias, Fame, Fortune , Violence and how the supernatural has cope and has faced this eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T14:19:30-08:00","id":364767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=364653#post364653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about it, a setting book for V:TM (and to a lesser extent, the others) set in Ancient Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about ancient Carthage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T14:23:36-08:00","id":364775,"title":"","content":"what i want (among other things) is a mage book that is nothing but one big list of rotes and&quot;how you do x&quot; and similar things. like i think mage awakening already has","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T18:13:15-08:00","id":364946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=364775#post364775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what i want (among other things) is a mage book that is nothing but one big list of rotes and&quot;how you do x&quot; and similar things. like i think mage awakening already has</div> </div> </div> </div>That is definitely something I DON'T want to see and would be the first Mage:anything I wouldn't buy. Ascension really couldn't decide what Rotes were or how they worked. Typically, they were paradigmatic window-dressing hung on a -1 Diff on an Arete role. At best they were good examples of the kind of thought that should be going into describing each and every effect.<br /> <br /> If they smooth out the Rote system and make into something more comprehensive, functional, consistent and robust in M20, then, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T19:05:56-08:00","id":364987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=364946#post364946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is definitely something I DON'T want to see and would be the first Mage:anything I wouldn't buy. Ascension really couldn't decide what Rotes were or how they worked. Typically, they were paradigmatic window-dressing hung on a -1 Diff on an Arete role. At best they were good examples of the kind of thought that should be going into describing each and every effect.<br /> <br /> If they smooth out the Rote system and make into something more comprehensive, functional, consistent and robust in M20, then, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>what's so different? if i recall in awakening a rote just gives more benefits than a scension but that's kinda it. nothing more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T19:32:27-08:00","id":365009,"title":"","content":"Settings are at the top of my list; it's criminal that we don't have <i>Dark Ages: Wraith</i> yet, and if <i>Victorian Age: Mage</i> is anything like that ancient outline you can find online, I'm very excited. Doesn't have to just be historical stuff, either; various city books are always great, and Wraith20's addition of several Necropoli (Rome!) has my beyond happy.<br /> <br /> Special mention goes to bucking the cWoD's horrid Eurocentric trend; I'd give anything to see some more Asian material that isn't hilariously anime or a racist trainwreck, but instead delves into the vast untapped history that is &quot;everywhere but Western Europe.&quot; Material for the Americas before European contact would be fascinating, especially for Wraith but with plenty of interesting options for <i>Vampire</i> and <i>Mage</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 01-09-2015, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T22:15:09-08:00","id":365113,"title":"","content":"I want a barbie and a pony.. and solom grondy want some pants!!!<br /> <br /> Technocracy: Another Brick in the Wall: A Setting book for operations set during the Cold War, From Cuba to USA to Moscow.<br /> <br /> Wraith: Deadsouls. A book on How to handle massive events whit hundreds of deads arriving to stygia.<br /> <br /> Translation Guide for: Prometheans on the 20 years settings.<br /> <br /> Moar April Fools Books (The Wraith Cookbook, one page only &quot;WRAITHS DONT EAT.&quot; )<br /> <br /> The Danger Roads of The Land of Dust, A Guide of Hitcchicking and Roadtrips by Old Man Many Skins. a book set on the Lost Highways of USA and in chronicles based on roadtrips and highways.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness: Urban legends - Creepy pasta edition.<br /> <br /> The Memoirs of a Smiling Bastard, A Tale by Smiling Jack.<br /> <br /> Wraith: The Doomslayer's (Un)Survivals Guide.<br /> <br /> To have a Foreword on a Changeling book written by Neil Gaiman <br /> <br /> A Brave New World: A book of What If Scenarios and Chronicles (Steampunk World of Darkness, Cyberpunk WoD, Space Opera World of Darkness, Anime World of Darkness, and what IF humans were aware of the supernatural and lived with these, and what if the WoD was more like a Pulp Fiction.)<br /> <br /> Wraith: Liberty, Equality, Fraternity or Death. A setting book for the French Revolution.<br /> <br /> Wraith: Tales from Stygia. Mystery, Horror, Noir chronicles set in the city of the dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T09:03:48-08:00","id":365464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=364767#post364767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about ancient Carthage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. It could be a setting adventure like Constantinople by Night where there's a slim possibility to save Carthage from its fate.The core book would be set before its fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T09:46:37-08:00","id":365483,"title":"","content":"I'd personally like the truth behind Carthage, in the VtM sense at least, to remain an uncertainty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T16:49:10-08:00","id":365857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=363881#post363881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> +1 for basically reading my mind on my wish list.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>^_^ Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=363990#post363990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few that I'd really like:<br /> <br /> 1.) Beckett's Jihad Diary to be done in volumes. Or even possibly as a sort of magazine, taking trips through the metaplot as the character likewise travels the world. This could even be expanded a bit to include a look at some of the other setting metaplots, too.<br /> <br /> 2.) A World of Darkness redone. A book that takes a look at the setting WoD and how it plays out all over the world, with some small hooks and tips about each.<br /> <br /> 3.) A WoD neutral Storyteller's Guide to Crossovers, and a smaller Player's Guide, focusing on tips and tricks, playstyles, and suggestions.<br /> <br /> 4.) I'd much rather see Hunter the Reckoning 20th than anything else that hasn't been officially announced yet, (Demon, Mummy, KotE, etc. . ) Not really sure if this counts, as much as I'd rather have it than any of the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like these suggestions. it's got my brain churning over all the possibilities. And your suggestion of having an independent WoD crossover Guide is pure genius. That neatly solves the issue of whether or not a system is being crossover friendly or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=365113#post365113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a barbie and a pony.. and solom grondy want some pants!!!<br /> <br /> Technocracy: Another Brick in the Wall: A Setting book for operations set during the Cold War, From Cuba to USA to Moscow.<br /> <br /> Wraith: Deadsouls. A book on How to handle massive events whit hundreds of deads arriving to stygia.<br /> <br /> Translation Guide for: Prometheans on the 20 years settings.<br /> <br /> Moar April Fools Books (The Wraith Cookbook, one page only &quot;WRAITHS DONT EAT.&quot; )<br /> <br /> The Danger Roads of The Land of Dust, A Guide of Hitcchicking and Roadtrips by Old Man Many Skins. a book set on the Lost Highways of USA and in chronicles based on roadtrips and highways.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness: Urban legends - Creepy pasta edition.<br /> <br /> The Memoirs of a Smiling Bastard, A Tale by Smiling Jack.<br /> <br /> Wraith: The Doomslayer's (Un)Survivals Guide.<br /> <br /> To have a Foreword on a Changeling book written by Neil Gaiman<br /> <br /> A Brave New World: A book of What If Scenarios and Chronicles (Steampunk World of Darkness, Cyberpunk WoD, Space Opera World of Darkness, Anime World of Darkness, and what IF humans were aware of the supernatural and lived with these, and what if the WoD was more like a Pulp Fiction.)<br /> <br /> Wraith: Liberty, Equality, Fraternity or Death. A setting book for the French Revolution.<br /> <br /> Wraith: Tales from Stygia. Mystery, Horror, Noir chronicles set in the city of the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh MY BUDDHA.... these are such Fantastic ideas Crowley. I really hope that some of these are ideas snatched up for Pitch day. If OP doesn't jump on these I hope that some intrepid writers here on the forums will write up these outlines as Fan made Supplements. There's just too many excellent games that could come from any one of these notions. I'm not sure if Neil Caiman is familiar with the Changeling RPG, but it would be a real treat if he said a few words on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:08:59-08:00","id":367759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=364946#post364946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is definitely something I DON'T want to see and would be the first Mage:anything I wouldn't buy. Ascension really couldn't decide what Rotes were or how they worked. Typically, they were paradigmatic window-dressing hung on a -1 Diff on an Arete role. At best they were good examples of the kind of thought that should be going into describing each and every effect.<br /> <br /> If they smooth out the Rote system and make into something more comprehensive, functional, consistent and robust in M20, then, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we're getting it anyway. There's going to be a &quot;How Do You Do That?&quot; guide for Mage. Not sure that it will be rotes, per se, but a list of Effects and how to create them. I'm all for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> I'll second an updated World of Darkness setting book - the first two are wildly outdated now.<br /> <br /> And I want a campaign for Mage. Something awesome that starts in Dark Ages, moves to Sorcerer's Crusade, then Victorian era, then modern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:44:59-08:00","id":367984,"title":"","content":"Tales of Magick: Space Opera.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or maybe just a Mirrors equivalent book for CWod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T19:35:58-08:00","id":368179,"title":"","content":"ok..This is hard but<br /> SOMEONE PLEASE RE EDIT THE WORLD OF DARKNESS COMIC BOOKS!!<br /> Vampire The Masquerade: Shipping Down To Boston: a one shot set during the european imigration to USA<br /> <br /> Wraith: Lights Camera Action, A one shot based on the Entertaiment industries within the world of the dead, and how Deadly can be to mess with undead actors, directors, stories that want to be told but are censored and the fiersome leader of Deadwood (The wraith hollywood), the leader of the Ratpack, Mister Frankie.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness: Anarchy in NY and Good Save The Queen. a one shot book using the Punk Rocker setting of the 60s and 70s for mage, werewolf and vampire. from characters of CBGBs, the Battle for CBGBs, New characters such as Travis McNeal an Irish vampire (intelligence2, brujah) sex driven, fast talker, wanker and claims to be the fifth sex pistol. and how did the Punk Rock affected the world of darkness<br /> <br /> Mage: All Along to The Watchtower: a One shot adventure featuring a roadtrip for Mage the ascension, set during the 1960s in where the mages are invited to take part of a massive ritual, a ritual that could change the world, and how the Technocratic union and the Nephandi try to avoid this..could our characters arrive to the &quot;Ritual of Love&quot; known as Woodstock?.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-13-2015, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:15:05-08:00","id":368825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that I think about it, a setting book for V:TM (and to a lesser extent, the others) set in Ancient Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=364767#post364767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that I think about it, a setting book for V:TM (and to a lesser extent, the others) set in Ancient Rome. How about ancient Carthage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Por que no los dos?<br /> <br /> I think both would be grand. Having the two cities, which were contemporaries and rivals, would really help flesh out the ancient vampire world.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T16:53:02-08:00","id":369161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=368825#post368825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Por que no los dos?<br /> <br /> I think both would be grand. Having the two cities, which were contemporaries and rivals, would really help flesh out the ancient vampire world.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not. When people think &quot;Ancient Rome&quot; they are not usually thinking of Republican Rome at the time of the Punic Wars. Most people would be looking for something a lot more grand and imperial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T17:46:02-08:00","id":369216,"title":"","content":"Besides Hunter the Reckoning 20, I'd love to see a 20th Anniversary Kindred of the East. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T22:12:33-08:00","id":369450,"title":"","content":"If someone makes a HtR20<br /> I DEMAND! a<br /> God45 War Journal.<br /> The Life in the Streets: A Guide for Rookie Hunters by Cop90<br /> Tales of Damnation and Redemption: A Guide for High Edges hunters, infernals and celestials.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Thomas Crowley Investigative Guide, A Co-Operation with Joe Torienark.: A small guide based on table meetings and reports on how do the Werewolf and Demon mythos and Lore would Fit.<br /> From the garou mythos point of view, from the Demon point of view, and then a mixed point of view<br /> <br /> Thomas Crowley Investigative Guide 2: A Cooperation with &quot;The Kid&quot;: a small guide between a Pooka and a Demon on how they mythos would fit, from the Changeling point of view, from the Demon point of view, and how the mythos of both demons and changelings would fit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Report 20192: The Blackbook</b></u><br /> <br /> This guide would START with the first 10 pages relating ANYTHING not related to the main subject from a tecnocratican point of view, either be reports of missing equipment, how to send a Supena to an Agent, Sheets of authorization for equipment.<br /> <br /> After wards we see a chapter titled &quot;The Right Procedure of Using Space Equipment for Biological Needs.&quot; next page, the same title but now with something written over saying &quot;<u><b>CLASSIFIED, FOR CONTROL EYES ONLY. ANY OTHER SUBJECT THAT IS NOT RELATED TO CONTROL WILL BE PUNISHED UNDER THE INTERNAL LAWS OF THE TECHNOCRATIC UNION. THIS MAY INCLUDE TERMINATION AND MEMORY ERASE.</b></u>&quot;<br /> Next page &quot;<i>Case File:</i> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Null Threat</b></u></span>.&quot; (a small cover and Hidden guide fo all the extraterrestrial and Null threat phenomenon and how to use it as a ST)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Human Guide to The World of Darkness: A small one shot detailing HOW IS the World of Darkness from a completely HUMAN point of view, what products can you buy from Pentex, what TV shows are people watching and such. i dont imagine it longer than 15 pages with some art involving people doing normal things (and maybe a supernatural in the background with out being noticed)<br /> <br /> Sins Bound in Blood: A book telling how does the world of darkness fits from the point of view of a Christian Zelot who wants to be a Hunter. Using elements from different world of darkness games and re telling it involving The Bible (something like How fanatics see the supernatural).<br /> <br /> Wraith The Oblivion Dead Air: A small adventure for Mortals within the Wraith's world. A bunch of guys start getting strange radio signals from someone crying like a wolf and playing strange old music, very twisted (with a bit of research, you can see they are actually songs). the adventure basically makes the Players help the ghost of a Radio DJ. the catch is that the DJ already accepted his role within stygia and now he is using the Radio to give shouts to the living world (and help one or other fella to deliver a message to their loved ones) as well to leave warning hidden within music to the livings and to what ever lies on the Dark Corners of the World (see it as a non sutil rouge council)<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampire: Centuries of Blood.<br /> A Guide for vampire the masquerade set in different eras , Greek, Rome, Egypt, Constantinople, Victorian Era, World War.<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Apocalypse: Ecchoes of the Caerns.<br /> A guide for Werewolf the apocalypse on how to set werewolf during the Roman Empire, Otoman Empire, Victorian Era, World War 1<br /> <br /> The Lost brothers.<br /> A guide for some of the Dead changing breed of werewolf (such as Camazots)<br /> <br /> Changeling: To The World's End<br /> A guide of changelings of south american mythologies (like Chileans traucos and invunches, brasilian, mexico, argentinian, peru, aztec, mayas etc...)<br /> <br /> The Final Hours of Vlad Tepees: a compilation of stories based on the final mortal days of vlad and what happend after he turned into a Vampire.<br /> <br /> The Gunpowder Plot: a one shot campaing for Mage the ascension set during The Gunpowder Plot.<br /> <br /> Seas of Blood: a one shot book for rules on Ship battles<br /> <br /> Active Targets: A sort of &quot;Red List&quot; book for Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Following Books are Intended as <b>Black Dog</b> books only. </span><br /> <br /> World of Darkness:Sects: A blackdog book for the New World of Darkness Cults and sects for Nephandi and other Satan worship creatures of the world of darkness<br /> <br /> Wraith The Oblivion: Massacres.: a book set on the Nephwracks born from &quot;Going Postal.&quot;, Haunting on High Schools and public massacres.<br /> <br /> Vampire the Masquerade: Dark Pleasures: A one shot story set on a Tzimisce/Sabbath Hellfire club, fill of taboos and sexual depravations involving ghouls and others.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness: Why dont you Bleed?: a Conversion book for Slashers on the Classic World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness: Only Gods Have Mercy: A one shot campaing set on a twisted hospital, a crossover adventure for Mage. Vampire or Wraith<br /> <br /> World of Darkness: Mindbreak: A setting for Mental Asylums on the World of Darkness (Both Corrupted and clear)<br /> <br /> Vampire the Masquerade: He Wept. a setting book for Jerusalem as well during the era of the crusifixions.<br /> <br /> Vampire the Masquerade: Blood And Vengeance: a one shoot adventure for Baalis and Salubri against the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Visions of Armaggedon: A book of different &quot;Reports&quot; and stories about the Apocalypse/Gehenna/Ascension/End Game/Winter etc... this is basically a throw off in case any ST wants to keep using the 'End of the World Incoming' sort of scenarios<br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Ok i think i went Pretty dark with the Black Dog games.... I need a shower, if any of the books suggested its WAY too controversial or &quot;Too Soon&quot; ill understand, if i need to be reprimended or caused any controversy ill understand and i will face it. im sorry if i hurted any sensibilities or &quot;Went too Far.&quot; My apologize if i made someone feel unconftable or unsettled with some of the things i suggested and if someone asks me to erase the list of Black Dog proposed books, ill comply and do it with out any problem or argument what so ever. I appreciate the comprehention.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-14-2015, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T08:29:40-08:00","id":369763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369161#post369161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, maybe not. When people think &quot;Ancient Rome&quot; they are not usually thinking of Republican Rome at the time of the Punic Wars. Most people would be looking for something a lot more grand and imperial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I don't think that should be a huge obstacle. Setting the story in fledgling Rome, while the Kindred really got their talons into the Republic before it became an Empire, sounds like a blast. I don't think it would be hard to get enough material to focus on a vampiric take on the Punic Wars. It might not necessarily be what people expect according to knee-jerk expectations of Ancient Rome, but it is an interesting and unexplored setting that I think has merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T14:33:39-08:00","id":370140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369450#post369450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith The Oblivion: Massacres.: a book set on the Nephwracks born from &quot;Going Postal.&quot;, Haunting on High Schools and public massacres.</div> </div> </div> </div>No thanks. I'm still unhappy with the existence of the Holocaust book; tapping anything more recent would be just as tasteless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T14:49:01-08:00","id":370150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=370140#post370140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No thanks. <b>I'm still unhappy with the existence of the Holocaust book</b>; tapping anything more recent would be just as tasteless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whaaaaaat? That was actually one of my favorite books for Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:00:51-08:00","id":370158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=370150#post370150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Whaaaaaat? That was actually one of my favorite books for Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a game out of the genocide of my family isn't exactly my idea of a good time. Neither is saying &quot;the Holocaust was just about Jews,&quot; and I say this as a Jew. I respect what the Wraith team was trying to do with <i>Charnel Houses</i>, I really do, but there was no way it could've come out well. Is it <i>G*psy</i> levels of terrible? Of course not, but it still never should've been published.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:32:11-08:00","id":370210,"title":"","content":"Im sorry if i caused any unconvienances with this. or any controversy, wasnt my intention. lets just..move on and talk other books please","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T16:11:22-08:00","id":370264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=370210#post370210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im sorry if i caused any unconvienances with this. or any controversy, wasnt my intention. lets just..move on and talk other books please</div> </div> </div> </div>You're totally fine, Crowley. My beef is with some of the old White Wolf crew, not you.<br /> <br /> Back on topic; how cool would a Dark Kingdom of Obsidian historical setting be? Set it before the coming of the Europeans and just exult in one of the coolest empires ever! Bonus points for some really nifty European arcanoi that we haven't seen before, and maybe explore how different Oblivion has to be in a setting where ritual murder is a perfectly mundane aspect of everyday life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T17:23:36-08:00","id":370382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=370158#post370158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making a game out of the genocide of my family isn't exactly my idea of a good time. Neither is saying &quot;the Holocaust was just about Jews,&quot; and I say this as a Jew. I respect what the Wraith team was trying to do with <i>Charnel Houses</i>, I really do, but there was no way it could've come out well. Is it <i>G*psy</i> levels of terrible? Of course not, but it still never should've been published.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm Jewish. My entire family as well. Great Grandmother was in the Holocaust. I never said it was supposed to be &quot;a good time.&quot; And of course the Holocaust wasn't &quot;just about the Jews.&quot; Who said this? I actually enjoyed the book, and I'm extremely glad it was published. I thought it was extremely daring for WW to release, and found it to be well-written as well. I think the writer of the book, Richard Dansky(praise the Wraith 20 based God) is Jewish, too. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying you must like it. We just have vastly different opinions on it. No worries. <br /> <br /> To each his/her own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 01-14-2015, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T22:48:30-08:00","id":370768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369161#post369161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, maybe not. When people think &quot;Ancient Rome&quot; they are not usually thinking of Republican Rome at the time of the Punic Wars. Most people would be looking for something a lot more grand and imperial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, but I think a broader book on Classical Antiquity that covers the Romans, Greeks, Persians, Carthaginians from about say the beginning of the Greco-Persian Wars in 499 B.C. and the end of the Third Punic War in 149 B.C. would be better than one about Rome at her height. Lots of conflict, different cultures, and different systems of government (especially with in Greece) with which to play with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human Guide to The World of Darkness: A small one shot detailing HOW IS the World of Darkness from a completely HUMAN point of view, what products can you buy from Pentex, what TV shows are people watching and such. i dont imagine it longer than 15 pages with some art involving people doing normal things (and maybe a supernatural in the background with out being noticed)</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be highly amusing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 01-15-2015, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T23:06:22-08:00","id":370774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=370382#post370382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm Jewish. My entire family as well. Great Grandmother was in the Holocaust. I never said it was supposed to be &amp;quot;a good time.&amp;quot; And of course the Holocaust wasn't &amp;quot;just about the Jews.&amp;quot; Who said this? I actually enjoyed the book, and I'm extremely glad it was published. I thought it was extremely daring for WW to release, and found it to be well-written as well. I think the writer of the book, Richard Dansky(praise the Wraith 20 based God) is Jewish, too. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying you must like it. We just have vastly different opinions on it. No worries. <br /> <br /> To each his/her own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think a line for what is acceptable gaming material has to be drawn somewhere; I put that pretty firmly at real-world genocide. You get added unpleasantness when people with no tie to the Holocaust get to play pretend; I think it's incredibly crass to make a book like Charnel Houses, because there's no guarantee individual tables with do it justice, and in the meantime you've given official sanction to all sorts of immature, offensive gaming groups.<br /> <br /> My other beef with Charnel Houses is how little it discusses how the Holocaust touched non-Jews; I don't remember anything about homosexuals, the handicapped, or Roma, yet they died just the same. <br /> <br /> I'm never going to come around regarding the book, and even if I respect the &quot;teach through play&quot; idea that motivated its creation, I don't trust the average group of roleplayers with handling such a horrific event (that's still within living memory and carries brutal aftershocks, especially in Eastern Europe), especially when the book itself is so flawed in the presentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T06:34:26-08:00","id":370927,"title":"","content":"guys, could we drop the discussion about what ever Charnel was ok or not?. im afraid some moderator will come and try to kill the conversation or threat someone<br /> <br /> <br /> A One shot for Wraith: Ashes And Cinder: a Book for wriaths of Pompei.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-15-2015, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T12:43:36-08:00","id":371358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369450#post369450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> World of Darkness: Why dont you Bleed?: a Conversion book for Slashers on the Classic World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked Slashers so a conversion book would be great. And also throw my vote in for a historical Dark Kingdom of Obsidian book as well.<br /> <br /> Antideluvian Rising: An alternate scenario book with scenarios where another anti rises instead of Ravnos. As well as a possible scenario (With a Whimper) where Caine has recently destroyed them. Thus, what does the Sabbat do when one of the biggest goals is now absolved?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> -An update of New Orleans and Berlin by Night given that the wall went down and the flood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 01-15-2015, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:39:23-08:00","id":371424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=370774#post370774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a line for what is acceptable gaming material has to be drawn somewhere; I put that pretty firmly at real-world genocide. You get added unpleasantness when people with no tie to the Holocaust get to play pretend; I think it's incredibly crass to make a book like Charnel Houses, because there's no guarantee individual tables with do it justice, and in the meantime you've given official sanction to all sorts of immature, offensive gaming groups.<br /> <br /> My other beef with Charnel Houses is how little it discusses how the Holocaust touched non-Jews; I don't remember anything about homosexuals, the handicapped, or Roma, yet they died just the same.<br /> <br /> I'm never going to come around regarding the book, and even if I respect the &quot;teach through play&quot; idea that motivated its creation, I don't trust the average group of roleplayers with handling such a horrific event (that's still within living memory and carries brutal aftershocks, especially in Eastern Europe), especially when the book itself is so flawed in the presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. I don't have that problem. Maybe I've been blessed to work with good roleplaying groups throughout the years. One of the reasons I love the World of Darkness is because it mirrors the real world so closely. Genocide is real. The Holocaust happened. And I thought it was handled with respect. My ST's always handled it with respect as well. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure the author intended it to be an encyclopedia of Holocaust victims and the effects it had on them. I don't think the author planned on having the book used in upper-class college courses, either. I look at the book as a tool to tell incredibly dark, fascinatingly mature role-playing games. That's what my group used it for. I want my games to be dark. I want my games to have meaning. I want my games to reflect the real world as much as possible. Probably why I can't get into any other role-playing games besides the material produced by OP/WW. As much as I'd like to enjoy Shadowrun, for example. <br /> <br /> I get what you're saying about immature groups. But I don't believe the role-playing groups that take the subject matter seriously should be prohibited from playing a game due to the role playing groups that do not. In fact, I'm of the opinion that I never want to see anyone not be allowed to do/enjoy &quot;something,&quot; just because that same &quot;something&quot; can be used against its purpose by fools. <br /> <br /> Whether it's mature videogames, table top rpgs, guns, sky-diving, etc. lol<br /> <br /> We won't see eye to eye on the subject, and like I said. No biggie. I'm just looking forward to more Wr20 goodness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:41:38-08:00","id":371425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=370927#post370927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">guys, could we drop the discussion about what ever Charnel was ok or not?. im afraid some moderator will come and try to kill the conversation or threat someone</div> </div> </div> </div>Relax. No one is getting into a flame war or insulting each other in the least. Everything is fine.<br /> <br /> I understand why Atamajjaki did not like Charnel Houses of Europe. And I've simply made my statement on why I did. <br /> <br /> Keep going with the ideas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T14:12:35-08:00","id":371446,"title":"","content":"Will Wr20 be covering Swar, India's dark kingdom? I always felt like it was super fascinating and deserved more love. Ditto for anywhere that isn't China (which does need a massive update) or Japan in the Dark Kingdo, of Jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:47:00-08:00","id":371539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=371358#post371358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Antideluvian Rising: An alternate scenario book with scenarios where another anti rises instead of Ravnos. <b>As well as a possible scenario (With a Whimper) where Caine has recently destroyed them. </b>Thus, what does the Sabbat do when one of the biggest goals is now absolved?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of boring though isn't it? All the big bads getting killed off screen is lame. Isn't that the core of most people's objection to the metaplot? Baba Yaga getting one shotted by the Nicktuku, Ravnos being killed by orbital technocracy lasers, and stuff like that that can never be affected by the players.<br /> <br /> If you want to do something with Caine, have him wake up and and be moving around. What's he doing? Looking for his granchilder? Siring new childer? Plotting to conquer the world? Plotting to save it from the Technocracy/Baali/Wyrm/whatever? Have the coterie investigate it.<br /> <br /> Hell, maybe the players could be his new childer. Maybe they know what they are, maybe they don't. Whatever the case, they have to survive without that being found out by the established kindred long enough to grow into their power and found their own clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 01-16-2015, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:56:29-08:00","id":371552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=371446#post371446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Wr20 be covering Swar, India's dark kingdom? I always felt like it was super fascinating and deserved more love. Ditto for anywhere that isn't China (which does need a massive update) or Japan in the Dark Kingdo, of Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure, but I don't think so. I agree with you, totally. And I love DKoJ. I was pleasantly surprised with the KS turnout. Figured Wraith wouldn't have much support in 2015, but I guess I was wrong. I wonder what new books will come out of it.<br /> <br /> Same with Changeling. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T17:21:41-08:00","id":371584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=371552#post371552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure, but I don't think so. I agree with you, totally. And I love DKoJ. I was pleasantly surprised with the KS turnout. Figured Wraith wouldn't have much support in 2015, but I guess I was wrong. I wonder what new books will come out of it.<br /> <br /> Same with Changeling.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You have no idea, dude. Wraith is a strong contender for my favorite game of all time; I was scared it wouldn't get funded at all, let alone make as much as it did. Fingers crossed for the strong showing with Wr20 to encourage a much-overdue Dark Ages: Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T18:41:35-08:00","id":371682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=371584#post371584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have no idea, dude. Wraith is a strong contender for my favorite game of all time; I was scared it wouldn't get funded at all, let alone make as much as it did. Fingers crossed for the strong showing with Wr20 to encourage a much-overdue Dark Ages: Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here, here. I thought we'd have to claw our way to get double the target goal by the end of the KS. Of course days after it started I saw I lengthy article about it on the Escapist, surprising the hell out of me and that's when I realized that it might just be more successful than I expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T21:41:14-08:00","id":371826,"title":"","content":"Worlds of Darkness: What if--<br /> - The Wod was set in a Victorian Steampunk era<br /> - The WoD was set in a Cyberpunk Era<br /> - Humanity Always knew about the supernatural and this was common to see. (Imagine Law and Order: Special Supernatural Unit, or to have an official Kindread President)<br /> <br /> Worlds of Darkness: Volume 2 What if...<br /> - The Supernatural creatures were Superheroes or SuperVillians (A small collab with the team behind Trinity)<br /> - The World of Darkness were to be a Space Opera pretty much like Star Trek/Star Wars or Asimov's The Foundation/ Firefly<br /> <br /> Worlds Of Darkness Volume 3: What if<br /> - Supernaturals were openly used during the World War 2.<br /> - The Supernatural element was caused due Transhumanism<br /> - Every Single Beeing in the planet was some sort of supernatural of the World of Darkness (No Humans Left)<br /> <br /> Worlds of Darkness Volume 4: What if<br /> - The Wyrm Had been defeated and the only standing force were Gaia/Khaos and the Weaver<br /> - The Weaver had been defeated and the only standing force were Gaia/Khaos and the Wyrm<br /> - Gaia/Khaos were defeated ant the only standing force were The Weaver and the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Worlds of Darkness Volume 5: What If....<br /> -Vampires never were to exist (and how the Wod Would have worked with out vampires)<br /> - Werewolfs/Shapeshifters never existed<br /> - Mages never existed<br /> - Wraiths never Existed<br /> <br /> Worlds of Darkness: More Worlds Than These.<br /> Due to some Umbral gate way:<br /> -Vampires of The Masquerade Faced Vampires of Requiem<br /> -Werewolves of Apocalypse Faced Werewolves from Forsaken<br /> -Wraiths faced Geists<br /> -Mages from the Ascension faced Mage the Awakened<br /> <br /> Ankoku no sekai:<br /> - What if every supernatural within the World of Darkness followed the Super Sentai or Magical Girl rules.<br /> - What if The Creatures (Garous, Kindread, Avatars and Wraiths) were some sort of Summoning creature using some sort of Game (Either Cards, Dices etc..)<br /> <br /> World of Darkness: What if: Total Control<br /> - What if the vampires were officially dominating human kind, with Blood Farms and humans were the &quot;Resistance.&quot;<br /> -What if Werewolves have overtake over the world and humans were The Resistance<br /> - What if Mages splitted the continents for the traditions and they took control, no technocracy but only the traditions and humanity fighting each other.<br /> -What if Spectres overun earth and there were enslaving humankind<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-16-2015, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T22:12:41-08:00","id":371879,"title":"","content":"Wow some of those are really awesome Crowley!<br /> <br /> Really like a lot of those ideas. Especially the Steampunk and WWII one.<br /> <br /> As for the President being Kindred, it would have to be a Toreador wouldn't it? Only they know the technique to use Presence through television IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T22:40:57-08:00","id":371917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=371879#post371879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow some of those are really awesome Crowley!<br /> <br /> Really like a lot of those ideas. Especially the Steampunk and WWII one.<br /> <br /> As for the President being Kindred, it would have to be a Toreador wouldn't it? Only they know the technique to use Presence through television IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks :P and the idea of the Aware WoD its mainly to run police type of scenarios (Thank you Wild Cards/Powers and Top 10 by alan moore)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T05:55:44-08:00","id":372226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=371539#post371539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to do something with Caine, have him wake up and and be moving around. What's he doing? Looking for his granchilder? Siring new childer? Plotting to conquer the world? Plotting to save it from the Technocracy/Baali/Wyrm/whatever? Have the coterie investigate it.<br /> <br /> Hell, maybe the players could be his new childer. Maybe they know what they are, maybe they don't. Whatever they case, they have to survive without that being found out by the established kindred long enough to grow into their power and found their own clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea. If the Assamites aren't trying to eat you, every other group might want you on their whether you like it or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T21:41:36-08:00","id":376909,"title":"","content":"I got Kindred of the East last year, and even though their culture is VERY ritual heavy (especially with their war-making), the Kuei-Jin seem to be a fascinating people. Sadly though, I find that the Year of the Lotus book-line is incomplete. To explain, let's see where every Supernatural race is technically:<br /> <br /> Vampire: Again Kindred of the East, check.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: Hengeyokai book, check.<br /> <br /> Mage: I know there's the Akashic Brotherhood, but I wonder if it's the ONLY tradition in the Middle Kingdom. I know, from a book on Chinese Fairy Tales, that there were two competing camps of thought: Confucianism and Taoism. Which school of thought is the Akashic Brotherhood? If that Tradition is one of these schools, then perhaps there should be a Tradition that reflects the other school, as a sort of rival to the Brotherhood. Also, are there any Eastern orientated Traditions that are exclusive to Asia? Ooo, how about a Tradition that takes advantage of ninja mysticism? It could be centered in the Inu(?) Prefecture, where it's claimed to be the birthplace of ninjas.<br /> Also, is Awakened culture in the Middle Kingdom different from Europe and America? How? Please consider making a Mages of the East book.<br /> <br /> Wraith: Thanks to the overwhelming response for Wraith20, the corebook will talk about the Jade Kingdom. Will everyone be okay with what's in the corebook or should Wraith get it's own Lotus book?<br /> <br /> Changeling: As far as I know, there's nothing about Changelings in the Middle Kingdom. Are their Asian-centric kiths or is Dreaming strictly Western only? If you can, consider making a Changelings of the East book for Dreaming fans, with also new Houses if allowed.<br /> <br /> Hunter: As far as I know, we have Demon Hunter X and Strike Team Zero, though I wonder about something. Are there any Imbued in Asia and if so what do they do for their Hunts? Are there any new Creeds that developed in the Middle Kingdom? I think there should be a Lotus book about Reckoning-type Hunters in Asia and how they Hunt there, What does everyone think?<br /> <br /> Mummy: The players guide on The Ten Thousand Immortals is great and detailed. I think that their culture should be expanded upon in their own Lotus book to make them as fulfilling as the Amenti (since the Middle Kingdom is the Asian Mummies territory). Are Shinto and Buddhist temples holy places to where the TTIs recuperate? What is their footprint in Asian history? What is their relations between the Kuei-Jin and the other shen? <br /> <br /> Demon: Asian Demons of the Yama Kings have been detailed in the book: The Ten-Thousand Hells. Is this book the Demon Lotus book? If not, might you make one to complete this order?<br /> <br /> The completion of the Lotus books is the only thing that I want to happen because it seems like that some game-lines became restricted geography-wise due to the classic WoD ending like that. Can Onyx Path make this happen in the future?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T22:38:07-08:00","id":376955,"title":"","content":"Regarding Mage and Asian stuff; I believe <i>Dragons of the East </i>covers Awakened society in Asia, primarily focused on the Akashic Brotherhood, Wu Lung, the local Technocrats, and a really unfortunate group of infernalists that I believe are no longer canon.<br /> <br /> Hunter and Mummy aren't likely to see anything until their respective anniversaries, which are both a ways off.<br /> <br /> Demon is specifically about fallen angels of the Christian god; the Yama Kings have nothing to do with them, though the Hells are described in <i>Dark Kingdom of Jade</i> for Wraith, which I highly recommend.<br /> <br /> I've been horribly vocal about my distaste for KotE, but I'd love a look at native Kindred who are actually, y'know, Kindred. The new African bloodlines in V20 Dark Ages give me hope that Onyx Path can do Asia justice where White Wolf failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T23:23:37-08:00","id":376999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=376955#post376955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Mage and Asian stuff; I believe <i>Dragons of the East </i>covers Awakened society in Asia, primarily focused on the Akashic Brotherhood, Wu Lung, the local Technocrats, and a really unfortunate group of infernalists that I believe are no longer canon.<br /> <br /> Hunter and Mummy aren't likely to see anything until their respective anniversaries, which are both a ways off.<br /> <br /> Demon is specifically about fallen angels of the Christian god; the Yama Kings have nothing to do with them, though the Hells are described in <i>Dark Kingdom of Jade</i> for Wraith, which I highly recommend.<br /> <br /> I've been horribly vocal about my distaste for KotE, but I'd love a look at native Kindred who are actually, y'know, Kindred. The new African bloodlines in V20 Dark Ages give me hope that Onyx Path can do Asia justice where White Wolf failed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't realize that there was a Lotus book for Mage. I thought it only covered Vampires, Werecreatures, ghosts, and Mortal Hunters. Is DotE on RPG Drive Thru?<br /> <br /> Also, the reason I wanted Onyx Path to create a Demons of the East book on the Yama Kings and the Akuma, was because of that exact reason. Sure the Judeo-Christian God and the Hevenly Host is an integral part of Western theology, but in the Middle Kingdom you have the Kami of Shintoism and Buddha. Hell, in KotE, there's an ACTUAL Asian GOD called the August Personage of Jade, which should've been just as important to the World of Darkness as God and his angels. To ignore the Yama Kings and the Akuma of the Middle Kingdom may give a wrong impression that the Akuma is not as important or was misinterpreted erroroneously as Judeo-Christian Fallen Angels instead. Not only is this a disservice, but it may insult players of that area to think that the company doesn't care about the Asian theater when it comes to Demon. By making the Akuma of the Middle Kingdom equal in stature to the Fallen, it opens up a lot and gives the Middle Kingdom the respect it deserves when it comes to its Demonology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T00:07:54-08:00","id":377021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=376999#post376999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I didn't realize that there was a Lotus book for Mage. I thought it only covered Vampires, Werecreatures, ghosts, and Mortal Hunters. Is DotE on RPG Drive Thru?<br /> <br /> Also, the reason I wanted Onyx Path to create a Demons of the East book on the Yama Kings and the Akuma, was because of that exact reason. Sure the Judeo-Christian God and the Hevenly Host is an integral part of Western theology, but in the Middle Kingdom you have the Kami of Shintoism and Buddha. Hell, in KotE, there's an ACTUAL Asian GOD called the August Personage of Jade, which should've been just as important to the World of Darkness as God and his angels. To ignore the Yama Kings and the Akuma of the Middle Kingdom may give a wrong impression that the Akuma is not as important or was misinterpreted erroroneously as Judeo-Christian Fallen Angels instead. Not only is this a disservice, but it may insult players of that area to think that the company doesn't care about the Asian theater when it comes to Demon. By making the Akuma of the Middle Kingdom equal in stature to the Fallen, it opens up a lot and gives the Middle Kingdom the respect it deserves when it comes to its Demonology.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/118/Dragons-of-the-East?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Google is your friend, dude. Took me four seconds.</a><br /> <br /> I believe it says somewhere that the August Personage of Jade <i>is</i> the same entity as God, at least in the oWoD. With that in mind, I suppose an argument could definitely be made for Fallen in Asia.<br /> <br /> While you haven't mentioned it specifically, Wraith gave more love to Asia than most of the other lines, and in a less racist way to boot (though it does suffer from the classic &quot;Asia is made up of China and Japan&quot; syndrome).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T04:18:44-08:00","id":377109,"title":"","content":"I was looking over my old emails and stumble upon an old (From november 2004) where I've inquired about the DA line and how every &quot;Modern Night&quot; line but 2 (Mummy and Wraith) had its DA equivalent DA: Vampire, DA: Werewolf, DA: Mage, DA: Fae (Changeling), DA: Inquisitior (Hunter), Devil's Due (Demon) and Blood and Silk (KOTE).<br /> <br /> I would love to see either a full fledge DA: Mummy and DA: Wraith core line or at least something like Devil's due and Blood and Silk for Mummy and Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T10:59:45-08:00","id":377365,"title":"","content":"ok, couple of quick shots rapid fire one shoot books.<br /> <br /> V20: What We Left Behind: A book dedicated to the Human side of the vampire, more important. Their families, and No, i dont mean other kindreads. i mean mother, father, siblings, sons and daughters and such, how do the different clans deal with loosing their loved ones, or how do vampires try to keep connected to these as well hidding their true nature<br /> as well for rules to play Childrens Embraced (How to roleplay a kid thats been turned into a vampire, both young and both ancient in a young kid's body) and rules for Vampire Pregnancy (What happend to those who are Embraced while pregnant..and no, i dont mean that the baby will be a Daywalker, i see it more as the baby vampire monster that appears on the Hunter's Survival Guide)<br /> <br /> W20: How i Met your Garou.: Another rapid fire book involving Family, how do garous understand their Human family. how do you ask your biological mother &quot;Ermm..why am i a werewolf?&quot;. touching subjects as family both inside and outside the caern (see it as garou kin and also as human kin). some examples (mainly using the family from Teen Wolf as an example) as well rules for reproduction between garous and kinfolks, how to make a human a kinfolk. rituals of pregnancy and garou marriage or partnership, how do tribes see this and how do garou families works (as well other changing breeds).<br /> <br /> <br /> M20: The Opening of The Chakras: ok...This is the Sex Book of Mage, basically how do traditions deal with sex as focus. the Kamasutra, The Tantra. Aliester Crowley, Nature and such.. taking for example things like Swamp Thing (The issue where The Swamp Thing and Tef\u00e9 Eat the Fruit) and how different procedures affect the focus or effects, from either beeing &quot;Love Making&quot; To &quot;Fucking&quot; to Ritualistic (Tantra, Kamasutra, Crowley's Style) and Root effects for sex (like avoid pregnancy) or others that can spawn due to this. as well the Traditions views on Sex<br /> <br /> M20: Its a Kind of Magic. Another quick one shot. How do mages cope with Families and siblings. How do you explain your parents or partner that you can create effects that alter reality?. How do mages settle down with families and childrens?. What are the views of the different traditions on having a family?. How does the technocracy act when two agents want to have a family or settle down? and how do marriage work in the Mage's Society. Each tradition point of view on: Marriage, Family , Who takes charge of the House and Childs. <br /> Rules for playing as Childs Mages (i have the theory that young kids are less suseptable to the paradox, similar to the Marauders)<br /> <br /> <br /> C20: Little Teeths: How do Changelings cope with having families, both in the Dreaming and as well in the banal world. How you involve yourself with your kids when youre a faery and how you sink the Belief in them? (examples beeing, using cantrips to play a Tooth Faery). How do Faes relate to having families and how do they handle this in the dreaming and in the banal world.<br /> <br /> Wraith20: The Things We Left Behind.<br /> Sometimes they arent a Wraith's passion but they are as important. How do wraiths cope with their families once they are gone, Do they keep an eye on them from &quot;The Other Side?&quot;. How do families cope with being Haunted by someone they loved and miss? How do wraiths and their childs interact -if they try to- and most important, how do wraiths try to avoid their loved ones for becoming ghosts like them?. as well, how does family protects each other (wraiths of relatives in Stygia).<br /> Rules for Kids being Mediums.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T17:47:20-08:00","id":377634,"title":"","content":"This thread it's full of good ideas!<br /> <br /> What I would like for M20:<ul><li>A new Masters of the Art, because it's universally hated (at least in part)-so this time it must be better.</li> <li>A Book of Traditions, similar to the new one of the Technocracy</li> <li>A new book of the Umbra, since Book of Worlds it's painfully old, and Infinite Tapestry its about the Avatar Storm. It should cover Horizon Realms, among other things.</li> <li>A book on Marauders, since we are having one about Nephandi.</li> <li>A book on Threat Null (this time with rules).</li> <li>A book on Ascension War. How it's fighted (treating particularly the issue of extending one's paradigm and fighting others), explaining the big players and their agendas, with a chronology with victories and losses of the factions, and how can you make a difference.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T19:32:08-08:00","id":377722,"title":"","content":"hey, would someone like me to writte one of the proposed one shots i got in there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T02:10:22-08:00","id":377901,"title":"","content":"JackalopeVegas, the problem with Hunter and Demon is that they came after the Year of The Lotus was over. They didn't exist when the project was running so they never got any coverage. Hunter would probably work mostly as is, with the possibility of a few extra creeds, but to be honest I don't really miss the Hunters all that much.<br /> <br /> Demon on the other hand does not work with KotE. In general the Demon line took a huge dump on all the metaphysics and backgrounds of all the other games (it's quite poor form to build up your heat by making everyone else seem like clueless idiots) and did its best bot to integrate peacefully with the other lines - which is quite contrary to the concept of Kindred of the East, which was made as a rather hollistic WoD where the factions interact and cooexist much more then in the vanilla lines. The Demons of eastern WoD are the Kuei Jin, the Akuma, the Bakemono, The Spirit servants of the Yama Kings, Banes and the Yama Kings themselves.<br /> <br /> Dragons of the East is a pretty cool book, and it covers a lot of the things you wanted:<br /> - The Five Metal Dragons - these guys are essentially a whole different paradigm of the Technocracy with a much more hollistic approach to Ascension which treats the Western Technocrats as their slightly stupid cousins. Also, they're quite aware they are doing magic.<br /> - Blind tunnel dwelling shamans of Vietnam<br /> - highly ritualistic shamans of Korea<br /> - The Dragon Wizards - Wu Lung<br /> - Akashic Brotherhood<br /> - Wu Keng - while these folks get a lot of bad rap, I really like them as antagonists, and even potentional PC's. They were given quite a bit of depth in this book and made quite a bit more even in their presentation. They are essentially peasant mages who as an act of desperation offered themselves to Demons so they could protect their own people. The end result is that they are men trained from childhood to act and dress as women so they could be the perfect brides to demons. They have some pretty cool visuals to their spells and have to edge the border between Infernal servitude and protecting their own people. One of the plots introduced here is that the demons have been lying to them all along and that they need but a little push to brake free<br /> - At least three different interpretations of what the ninjas are and are not, and one Craft that's essentially the modern ninja - Go Kamisori Gama<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T03:50:31-08:00","id":377939,"title":"","content":"Wu Keng are all sorts of unpleasant and I'm glad they're confirmed to not be coming back in M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>