","edited":{"userid":5259,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5259-accordiontoplan","user":"Accordiontoplan","date":".  Typos 03-07-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5259-accordiontoplan","name":"Accordiontoplan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T09:54:11-08:00","id":431324,"title":"","content":"In addition to the MtSC: Witches and Pagans Pod book...<br /> <br /> ... I would like a book summarizing the metaplot from cWoD from all supernaturals' points of view (if possible) to be located in one resource. Considering all the books that have been printed with the on-going plot (which I have many), I recognize that every specific detail cannot be included in such a tome. All the existing supplements can be used to &quot;fill in the blanks&quot; for specific details, but an overarching summary would give me a better understanding of how to set up a cWoD campaign faithful to the overall story set in the 90's to early 00's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5259,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5259-accordiontoplan","user":"Accordiontoplan","date":". 03-07-2015, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5259-accordiontoplan","name":"Accordiontoplan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:56:12-08:00","id":431499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accordiontoplan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=431324#post431324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to the MtSC: Witches and Pagans Pod book...<br /> <br /> ... I would like a book summarizing the metaplot from cWoD from all supernaturals' points of view (if possible) to be located in one resource. Considering all the books that have been printed with the on-going plot (which I have many), I recognize that every specific detail cannot be included in such a tome. All the existing supplements can be used to &amp;quot;fill in the blanks&amp;quot; for specific details, but an overarching summary would give me a better understanding of how to set up a cWoD campaign faithful to the overall story set in the 90's to early 00's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beckett's Jyhad Diary will do this for V20; I can imagine similar books for other lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:15:04-08:00","id":431526,"title":"","content":"I like Turtles..<br /> <br /> Anyone else thinks a setting book for the Cold War would be interesting? mainly for Mage<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:43:16-08:00","id":431802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=431499#post431499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary will do this for V20; I can imagine similar books for other lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be released mid-2015. Excellent!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5259-accordiontoplan","name":"Accordiontoplan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:31:45-07:00","id":433047,"title":"","content":"Hunter the Reckoning 20th Anniversary Edition.<br /> <br /> The Deluxe KS edition can have a cover with diecut bullet holes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T15:14:08-07:00","id":433190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=433047#post433047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter the Reckoning 20th Anniversary Edition.<br /> <br /> The Deluxe KS edition can have a cover with diecut bullet holes.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had lots of guns and fire the last time, and it didn't necessarily fit so well. Maybe it should have a kind of dual-cutaway view, like you're looking through one of the lenses from They Live, but it's only halfway over your eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:42:54-07:00","id":433398,"title":"","content":"<b>Sorcerer 20</b>: an update of the 1997 <b>World of Darkness: Sorcerer</b> supplement that set hedge magicians up as something distinct from and independent of mages. Suitable for use with any of the reborn World of Darkness gamelines or as a standalone game in its own right. Distinctly <i>not</i> done as a M20 supplement: guidelines for using it with M20 should be included, but with no more emphasis than the guidelines for using it with V20, W20, Wr20, or C20. <br /> <br /> Mechanics from SRev can be used when they\u2019re an improvement over the first edition, or as optional rules; but SRev-based setting material should be confined to the Sorcerer/Mage crossover notes. More generally, I want to see simple and streamlined rules (on par with <b>Hunters Hunted II</b>\u2019s Hedge Magic rules) as the baseline, with any additional complications included as clearly delineated options. <br /> <br /> Focus the book exclusively on Hedge Magic; but include as a KS stretch goal a supplement for psychics \u2014 something that sets <i>them</i> up as something distinct from and independent of both mages and sorcerers, with their own theme and mood and enough psychic-specific setting material to enable all-psychic chronicles. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> I could also go for a <b>M20 Ascension\u2019s Right Hand</b>, which would be to M20 as <b>Hunters Hunted II</b> is to V20. I would <i>not</i> expect it to flesh out Hedge Magic to the same extent that <b>Sorcerer 20</b> would, or even to the same extent as the original Sorcerer supplement; but I\u2019d also expect it to have a much broader scope, covering custos of <i>all</i> kinds: hedge wizards, psychics, the faithful, demon-pacted mortals, acolytes, sleeper assistants whose only benefit is that they don\u2019t count as witnesses to a particular mage\u2019s style of magic, etc. Also Familiars and artificial lifeforms (golems, clones, robots, etc.), and crossover notes for other gamelines: that is, a section that talks about things like werecats, ghosts, or changelings who serve as custos or otherwise participate in <b>Mage</b> society. <br /> <br /> In short, a book about non-mage characters in <b>M20</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  formatting error 04-14-2015, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T19:12:28-07:00","id":433443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=433190#post433190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We had lots of <b>guns</b> and fire the last time, and it didn't necessarily fit so well. Maybe it should have a kind of dual-cutaway view, like you're looking through one of the lenses from They Live, but it's only halfway over your eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any guns on the covers of any HtR books are not visible from a book shelf. And the main book never had guns. Just shell casings.<br /> <br /> <br /> And speak for yourself! The Hunter the Reckoning books and their wonderful fire adorning covers look amazing on my shelf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T19:50:10-07:00","id":433487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=433443#post433443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any guns on the covers of any HtR books are not visible from a book shelf. And the main book never had guns. Just shell casings.<br /> <br /> <br /> And speak for yourself! The Hunter the Reckoning books and their wonderful fire adorning covers look amazing on my shelf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>it would be nice if a special edition only had a dark cover and the symbol for MDG/Hunt in red.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T21:19:20-07:00","id":433564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=433443#post433443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any guns on the covers of any HtR books are not visible from a book shelf. And the main book never had guns. Just shell casings.<br /> <br /> <br /> And speak for yourself! The Hunter the Reckoning books and their wonderful fire adorning covers look amazing on my shelf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're lobbing me softballs. The art in Reckoning was infamous for not lining up with the realities of the setting. Maybe they'll meet halfway in the anniversary edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T07:27:08-07:00","id":433990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=433564#post433564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're lobbing me softballs. The art in Reckoning was infamous for not lining up with the realities of the setting. Maybe they'll meet halfway in the anniversary edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh...I'm not trying to &quot;lob&quot; you anything.<br /> <br /> I was talking about the cover. The cover for the main book. With the fire. And the shells. And...that's it.<br /> <br /> And I thought the art in general, across the entire line, may have started off like the Punisher--with guns blazing from every corner inside every page. But got significantly better as time went on across its 20+ books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:09:20-07:00","id":463603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=433190#post433190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We had lots of guns and fire the last time, and it didn't necessarily fit so well. Maybe it should have a kind of dual-cutaway view, like you're looking through one of the lenses from They Live, but it's only halfway over your eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I deeply believe that Vampire: The Masquerade would have never be the success it was without Tim Bradstreet's powerful art. And HtR suffered horribly from lackluster art, which contradicted much of the mood the text tried to inspire. In a page you would read Hunters are the everymen/women of the world, they are not 4-colours superheroes, then the art of the rest of the chapter would go on showing badly drawn cast outs from Blade comics. <br /> <br /> If we ever reach the point of H20, PLEASE use the art from Wayward and Hermit Hunter Books!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4288-caernkeeper","name":"Caernkeeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:43:30-07:00","id":463955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caernkeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=463603#post463603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I deeply believe that Vampire: The Masquerade would have never be the success it was without Tim Bradstreet's powerful art. And HtR suffered horribly from lackluster art, which contradicted much of the mood the text tried to inspire. In a page you would read Hunters are the everymen/women of the world, they are not 4-colours superheroes, then the art of the rest of the chapter would go on showing badly drawn cast outs from Blade comics.<br /> <br /> If we ever reach the point of H20, PLEASE use the art from Wayward and Hermit Hunter Books!!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I'll agree that some of the art of HtR was pretty bad, not all of it was. <br /> <br /> The Glenn Fabry covers, in particular, were nothing short of amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T03:07:45-07:00","id":471044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=463955#post463955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While I'll agree that some of the art of HtR was pretty bad, not all of it was.<br /> <br /> The Glenn Fabry covers, in particular, were nothing short of amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. But the chapter art, man!<br /> The Hunter Line hit their stride artwise during the Creedbooks. I hope the H20 development team acknowledges that and address this harmony issue between text and art. In short lived lines such as Demon adn Hunter, they can squeeze basically all the line in one great book - and I mean great not only in big. <br /> <br /> In H20 I hope they explore more of the flavor of isolation x hope in forms of Backgrounds. Twin Soul, Animal Companion, Bystander INSTEAD of your regular Contacts and Allies as the chronicle progresses, and the hunters alienate themselves from regular society. Subtle changes like that. <br /> <br /> In D20 the possibilities are even juicier! Rituals and Bastions in the main book?! Great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4288-caernkeeper","name":"Caernkeeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T10:32:58-07:00","id":471362,"title":"","content":"Ahh..Hunter20 (or hunter 15)<br /> a dream to come, honestly what i would love its if they mention how the hunters and hunter net has evolved. the usage of Twitter and such).<br /> <br /> As for D20: the only thing i want its to give a sort of clear explanation on the relation between demons and some of the supernaturals from its origin. im investigating on the Baali's and im still dumfounded when it comes to The Children and the Demon Lore.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T11:59:02-07:00","id":471409,"title":"","content":"I just want Guy Davis to come back to illustrate more Wraith and Dark Ages stuff.<br /> <br /> ...speaking of which, I'd kill for Dark Ages: Wraith to finally happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:35:34-07:00","id":479432,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">For Vampire: The Masquerade</span><br /> <br /> <b>Clanlessbook: Caitiff</b> - I want to write this book myself. Examining unlife as the bottom feeders and dumpster-sleepers, harried and hounded by the scourge, the second-class citizens of the Camarilla, the proud stooges of the Sabbat, the first casualties of the Jyhad, and how they survive night to night. All told in far more detail than Outcasts or Time of Thin Blood, and detailing the Caitiff's responses to the persecution of the Final Nights.<br /> <br /> <b>Guide to the Inconnu</b> - In a similar vein to <b>VII</b> for Vampire: The Requiem, a book presenting three or so different versions of what the Inconnu <i>might </i>be in the World of Darkness, as well as guidelines for creating your own spin on the mysterious sect. Would include the known history of the Inconnu during the nights of Ancient Rome.<br /> <br /> <b>Jus Sanguinis: A Guide to the Bloodlines</b> - A book that gives each of the minor bloodlines a bit more depth and history.<br /> <br /> <b>Wages of Sin</b> - A book focusing on Necromancy, to help bring it up to the level of Thaumaturgy in terms of Paths and Rituals. More information on the Underworld as presented in Vampire (with obvious shout-outs to Wraith).<br /> <br /> <b>V20 Storyteller's Compendium </b>- Something along the lines of the 1st Edition Storyteller's Handbook - with advice on storytelling, crafting chronicles and the like of course, but focusing on painting outside the lines presented in the existing rulebooks. System permutations and alternatives, ways to incorporate elements of other WoD games, ways to alter the setting (whether in geography or chronology), and other fun stuff to get people brainstorming on how to make the V:tM setting their own.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">For Demon: The Fallen &amp; Wraith the Oblivion</span><br /> <br /> <b>The Harrowing:</b> A re-imagining of Hell in the World of Darkness so that it's not so... well... boring. Instead of having demons more or less all standing around in an empty room being bitchy to each other, give us Hell as a setting. It doesn't have to be all Judeo-Christian, but we need something more than &quot;God stuffs you in a bag of holding.&quot; Perhaps Hell was originally a void... but as the eons passed and the great Wheel turned, cracks began to form at the periphery, allowing the weakest of demons to touch the darkest recesses of the Shadowlands and draw in plasm for use in constructing a new world, a perverted mirror of the Heaven that birthed the Demons.<br /> <br /> I have images of Spectres and Wraiths who fall too deep into a Harrowing brushing up against the fracturing wall of Hell, where monstrous, impish clawed arms flail and grasp at them - possibly pulling them through the barrier and into the hands of Demons who have been waiting ages to have <i>something </i>to mold and shape... where the last thing the Wraith sees are the spires of cities built upon the plasm of the darkest of human souls. Or perhaps the Damned Soul is dragged into a coffer where his soul and the souls of other Damned are bartered as currency - whether as raw materials, slave labor or perhaps entertainment for a noble of the Demon courts.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this version of Hell is only a pocket in the deepest, darkest pits of the Umbra, where a small number of demons have managed to slip through and forge an overlapping plane between Hell and the Shadow - a sort of grand trick to grant them some illusory semblance of freedom, where the &quot;gravity&quot; of hell doesn't pull them, but where they can once again create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:23:49-07:00","id":488430,"title":"","content":"Orpheus<br /> Mirrors for cWoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T09:55:07-07:00","id":493708,"title":"","content":"I'm going to second Dataweaver's suggestion on a new <b>Sorcerer </b>Supplement. I would definitely like some hints at incorporating them beyond Mage. (Tremere Ghouls, Uktena Kinfolk, or as adversaries.) I also think that <b>Psychics </b>could get their own book, or at least a dedicated section of the book, as well as a segment on where the two meet. (An example being Via Ignis from the old Inquisition book, which seems to be a Psychic power amongst their rituals. Other possibilities would be a Shapeshifter developing Biocontrol or Animal Psi, or a Pyrokenetic learning Hellfire to better control his abilities.)<br /> <br /> Summoning, Enchantment, and Alchemy could also use a little love and attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:00:27-07:00","id":513275,"title":"","content":"DA: Fae Modern Era<br /> <br /> Changeling Translation Guide<br /> <br /> Porting Promethean, Geist, and Beast in the CWoD<br /> <br /> NWoD and CWoD crossover book.<br /> <br /> New Supernatural splats like Djinn, Asura, Yokai, Xian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","name":"TunnelsofDarkness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:09:10-07:00","id":513347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=513275#post513275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DA: Fae Modern Era</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have to be presented as a Shard of the original World of Darkness; but yeah. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=513275#post513275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling Translation Guide</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, please. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=513275#post513275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Porting Promethean, Geist, and Beast in the CWoD</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d much rather get oWoD counterparts, even if not as full gamelines. For <b>Promethean</b>, I'd want a <b>Mage</b> supplement dedicated to constructs as the protagonists; for <b>Geist</b>, I'd want a <b>Wraith</b> supplement that exists in a space somewhere between <b>Risen</b> and <b>Orpheus</b>, or a sort of supercharged variant of <b>Mediums</b>. I haven't seen enough of <b>Beast</b> to form an opinion yet. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=513275#post513275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NWoD and CWoD crossover book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I follow. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=513275#post513275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Supernatural splats like Djinn, Asura, Yokai, Xian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given their track record with Gypsies and Kuei-Jin, I'd rather not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World