that felt anything needed to be changed. But I understand that there were many that did, and I feel that OP has handled such topics very, very delicately.<br /> <br /> Kindred of the East 20, for example, could be an extremely awesome thing under the OP umbrella. Especially with a few updates and changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 05-14-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T23:00:42-07:00","id":513857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=513468#post513468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stop. Seriously.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'll add a bit more. I'm fully confident in Eddy's, David's, Dave's, Rich's, and pretty much everyone in the Onyx Path crew to not make the same &quot;mistakes&quot; a different company made 15+ years ago.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I was never one of those that felt anything needed to be changed. But I understand that there were many that did, and I feel that OP has handled such topics very, very delicately.<br /> <br /> Kindred of the East 20, for example, could be an extremely awesome thing under the OP umbrella. Especially with a few updates and changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair bit of any potential for future cleanup on the KotE front involves how Wraith handles paradigms of death in Wr20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T17:04:07-07:00","id":514627,"title":"","content":"I'd like a <b>Kindred of the East: the Great Leap Outward</b> sourcebook. The Great Leap Outward - a.k.a the kuei-jin invasion of California - was <i>the</i> defining event for an entire generation of kuei-jin. It brings them (in force) to the West for the first time, putting them in direct contact/conflict with Western supernaturals. It allowed the young ones to escape the reach of their elders, gives the Bamboo Princes room to maneuver . . .and its the first thing the Quincunx was able to agree on in centuries.<br /> <br /> And it was an incredibly dynamic time for . . .well, everyone. Borders were changing nightly, San Diego returns to the Camarilla, and one ticked-off elder (or mandarin) could plunge an entire city back into war. <br /> <br /> A major crossover event, lots of potential for adventure and advancement . . .and yet White Wolf broke up the events among something like a dozen city and splatbooks. You'd get a line in one book about how the kuei-jin were on the verge of attacking, and then, in the next, they'd be talking about how Monkey Trip Wu was planning on naming the seized territory the &quot;Quicksilver Court&quot;. Then, in a third, you'd get a brief mention about how he'd botched the ancestor rite . . .<br /> <br /> Such a seminal event deserves its own sourcebook. It wouldn't even have to be updated for 20th anniversary - it'd be great to be able to play a wu in the first wave - or during the heady days of their early victories. Things are in such flux, it'd give Storytellers a lot of freedom. Just pick (or create) a mandarin to lead the assault (on a particular city), and start the campaign with the first moments of the assault, as the kuei-jin erupt from the ship's hold. . . <br /> <br /> And you could crossover with so many other settings - unlike Cainites, kuei-jin know <i>exactly</i> what to do with caerns/nodes/haunts/freeholds . . . And so many of the resident supernaturals are just <i>so</i> tasty . . .<br /> <br /> Plus, if Onyx Path <i>does</i> want to add in 20th anniversary material, there's plenty of opportunity there, too. We never did get much on the &quot;New Promise Mandarinate&quot; (kuei-jin California) under Han Hui, for example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T16:27:28-07:00","id":517397,"title":"","content":"<br /> When I first saw this thread, my initial reaction was, Changeling - Changeling - Changeling<br /> Then I read a few of the responses, and saw many of the same ideas I had, have been posted<br /> most Notably:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#696969\">Originally posted by <b>Darling_Rose</b><br /> My Wishlist goes something like this.<br /> <br /> C20</span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#696969\">The lost Book of Glamour and Kithbook Boggan</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\">New setting books for All the kingdoms. Pacifica, Apples, Willows, Northern Ice, ALL of them.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\">A mini-book like the Silver Record, or the Book of Nod, a little leatherette piece for Changelings on Fae History. (Ahem, all in Shakespearean pentameter)</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\">Revised Books of Houses maybe all in one Volume</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\">Expanded Kithbooks all around. Maybe also all in one Volume. Maybe rules for making/ Adapting new Kith</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\">New and expanded rules for the Dreaming and what goes on there.</span></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the 3 lost books from Changeling the Dreaming were my reflexive thoughts.<br /> - The Book of Glamour (I'm hoping is Stretch Goal #1 for the 20th edition)<br /> - Kithbook Boggan (or even better, a Book of Kithain stretch Goal which includes Boggan - think also Pixies &amp; Sprites)<br /> - Keys to the Kingdom (which served as story for the year of the Scarab, as well, Egypt &amp; the Amazon - Changeling/Mummy crossover, and more)<br /> - Yes, a mini Silver Record/Book of Nod esque peice on Fae history in its beginnings would be a fascinating read<br /> - A revised Shadow Court edition for 20<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#696969\">Originally posted by <b>Darling_Rose</b><br /> My Wishlist goes something like this.<br /> <br /> M20</span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#696969\">M20 Traditions Gathered + Guide to the Traditions</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\">M20 Conventions Gathered + Guide to the Conventions.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\">M20 Digital Web ?.0 + Infinite Tapestry + Horizon</span></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><br /> - all of these would be very useful books<br /> - M20 Book of Crafts - Dead Magic 1 &amp; 2 - Book of Lost Paths Compendium<br /> - I would also add the Book of Worlds to the Infinite Tapestry<br /> <br /> WtA20<br /> - Book of the Weaver (which would make a great cross reference to M20 Technocracy)<br /> - Book of the Wyld (with C20 coming, this would be a great crossover book, as their origins are essentially of the Wyld)<br /> - Bunyip (as previously mentioned by another)<br /> <br /> <br /> V20<br /> - Inconnu (someone previously posted this, and here is my agreeing)<br /> <br /> WtO20<br /> - Skinlands (it would be great to see a full book dedicated to crossover possibilities with all of the other cWod settings)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6040,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","user":"Quiet Storm","date":". 05-18-2015, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T21:13:42-07:00","id":517620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=517397#post517397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtA20<br /> - Book of the Weaver (which would make a great cross reference to M20 Technocracy)</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd get weird if you tried to use a Werewolf book with Mage. There's a lot between Werewolf and Mage that doesn't line up, and by default, Werewolf would assume that neat gadgets get shut down completely by Jam Technology, Gremlins and the like with no chance to resist unless a technocrat happened to be skilled in Spirit. Since, as a general rule, access to Dimensional Science is highly restricted, confrontations with Garou and Fera would not end up particularly well for technocratic agents, or even their dupes. Just one use of an innocuous Gift, and all the members of a SF0 team start going out of their mind when they see a character in Crinos. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Book of the Wyld (with C20 coming, this would be a great crossover book, as their origins are essentially of the Wyld) </div> </div> </div>The Triat generally doesn't play well with crossover, honestly. In the case of the Wyld, it's because everything is a one-off and nothing is necessarily related. It used to work in a way that was conducive to Fae; it doesn't any more, because to do so would be to remain the same, and that's just not its bag.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T22:18:15-07:00","id":517650,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy is pretty much the Weaver.<br /> <br /> Give everything a name, and conform it.<br /> Make it so it stays in its place.<br /> Remove anything that does not fit.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy wants to keep everything as mundane as possible. It is a direct correlation to what the purpose is the Weaver represents. A book that crosses over would show how influential the primitive forces actually are with regards to the other game lines.<br /> <br /> As stated at a Gen Con Onyx Path podium conference (direct quote), &quot;You don't want a Werewolf showing up in your Living Room, well, that's what the Technocracy is there for&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which coincidentally, is what the Weaver is all about.<br /> <br /> I think Fae &amp; the Wyld are as closely related as ever (unless you're referring to the Lost).<br /> <br /> The Wyld grows in a chaotic fashion, unchecked, and free form. This is the premise of what Changeling the Dreaming is supposed to be. Removing itself from the coils of restriction, and growing out into the Wyld. Remembering its true Nature, waking out form its dream state, and being apart of the ever growing -- its struggles against human perception &amp; the doldrums of the Autumn People, as well the plight of the Shadow Court.<br /> <br /> This could be a fantastic crossover.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T22:33:42-07:00","id":517658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd get weird if you tried to use a Werewolf book with Mage. There's a lot between Werewolf and Mage that doesn't line up, and by default, Werewolf would assume that neat gadgets get shut down completely by Jam Technology, Gremlins and the like with no chance to resist unless a technocrat happened to be skilled in Spirit. Since, as a general rule, access to Dimensional Science is highly restricted, confrontations with Garou and Fera would not end up particularly well for technocratic agents, or even their dupes. Just one use of an innocuous Gift, and all the members of a SF0 team start going out of their mind when they see a character in Crinos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, technically, not all Technocratic procedures are empowered by &quot;technology&quot;, as werewolves understand it.<br /> <br /> Mental conditioning (to resist the delirium) isn't done via implanted, electronic, gadgets, and, really, isn't always done with chemicals either. Never heard of Gifts to Jam Psychology/Sociology. Can these Gifts that you mention jam chemicals (that already have been used) as well as they do with machinery ? if they don't then, your argument here it's pointless.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's GENERALLY a bad idea to battle gun-to-claw with the werewolves (<i>for anyone,</i> mage, vampire, fomori or whatever) , but technocrats are crafty, and can surely find a way to even the odds, if they have enough reason to bother. If Pentex can do it, Technocrats will find a way too.<br /> <br /> Much better to point how 3\u00ba edition mages aren't related any more to the Triat (as they used to be). Or how the usual ineptitude with Spirit/DiCi in general and the Middle Umbra in particular makes very hard for technocrats to truly comunicate to the Weaver (even when they're doing Her work, by controlling magick, expanding stasis, etc... That you don't believe in the Weaver doesn't mean that the Weaver doesn't believe in you...). <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld grows in a chaotic fashion, unchecked, and free form. This is the premise of what Changeling the Dreaming is supposed to be. Removing itself from the coils of restriction, and growing out into the Wyld. Remembering its true Nature, waking out form its dream state, and being apart of the ever growing -- its struggles against human perception &amp; the doldrums of the Autumn People, as well the plight of the Shadow Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's true that The Dreaming it's ever changing, and wild beyond even the comprehension of changelings (who are supposed to be its guardians) . It's surely related to the Wild in a crossover, or at least Werewolves will likely see it as such, if they travel there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-18-2015, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T23:24:11-07:00","id":517702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=517658#post517658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, technically, not all Technocratic procedures are empowered by &quot;technology&quot;, as werewolves understand it.<br /> <br /> Mental conditioning (to resist the delirium) isn't done via implanted, electronic, gadgets, and, really, isn't always done with chemicals either. Never heard of Gifts to Jam Psychology/Sociology. Can these Gifts that you mention jam chemicals (that already have been used) as well as they do with machinery ? if they don't then, your argument here it's pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description of the Gift, Jam Technology, specifies that if affects &quot;any devices shaped from fabricated materials such as metal or plastic.&quot; It goes on to mention that it can prevent gunpowder from igniting, so it might work against the drugs (since it's hampering chemical reactions of fabricated objects in this sense, at least if the effect is ongoing), but conditioning isn't within the purview of the Gift at all. For those stalwarts, you would use something like Shadows of the Impergium or Terror of the (ugh) Dire Wolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, it's GENERALLY a bad idea to battle gun-to-claw with the werewolves (<i>for anyone,</i> mage, vampire, fomori or whatever) , but technocrats are crafty, and can surely find a way to even the odds, if they have enough reason to bother. If Pentex can do it, Technocrats will find a way too. </div> </div> </div>You generally just don't even engage in that situation, I'd imagine. That's why you get things like Dead Man's Hand (well-funded ex-military types who are mysteriously immune to the Delirium), or why they'd try to lobby Pentex to send in First Teams. Pentex knows about those kind of RDs, after all. Perhaps a bit too well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Much better to point how 3\u00ba edition mages aren't related any more to the Triat (as they used to be). Or how the usual ineptitude with Spirit/DiCi in general and the Middle Umbra in particular makes very hard for technocrats to truly comunicate to the Weaver (even when they're doing Her work, by controlling magick, expanding stasis, etc... That you don't believe in the Weaver doesn't mean that the Weaver doesn't believe in you...). <hr /> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that follows. Technocrats, if they interact with Werewolf at all, would be Weaver-ish by... (sunglasses) coincidence. (meetthenewbossclip.mp3)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, it's true that The Dreaming it's ever changing, and wild beyond even the comprehension of changelings (who are supposed to be its guardians) . It's surely related to the Wild in a crossover, or at least Werewolves will likely see it as such, if they travel there. </div> </div> </div>The Dreaming is a thing aside from the Umbra, according to W20 Umbra. It definitely doesn't feel familiar to Changers. Also, Changelings have a reputation for screwing around with Garou and Fera in ways that can be lethal, so the shapeshifters developed a rite to savage the areas where the fae realms and the Umbra meet, kick down the door, and leave the ragged hole as a chimare-spewing warning (Rend Trod).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-18-2015, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T23:38:41-07:00","id":517707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=517702#post517702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about the cosmology of a Werewolf book here. While some of the Umbra got rearranged, Consensus is very much a thing that can sit and spin, which means that there is a very keen divide between magic and technology. Technocrats wouldn't be magic(k)al willworkers in the sense that Werewolf describes things, and since this is a hypothetical W20 Book of the Weaver and not M20 Technocracy we're talking about, that's what you'd go with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under those conditions, I'd rather not talk about the Technocracy at all. Weaver Technology, sure (which is different from both mundane technology and Enlightened Hypertech); and the original Book of the Weaver talked a bit about \u201cDrone mages\u201d who had trouble with Vulgar magic but had built-in regenerative powers (\u201cresetting\u201d to an undamaged state). But leave the Technocracy itself out; or at least limit yourself to something to the effect of \u201cthere\u2019s a group of technomancers that the Weaver generally approves of\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T03:10:21-07:00","id":517796,"title":"","content":"Actually the Technocracy are by no means servants of the Weaver. The original 1st edition Technocrats were faceless agents of static reality with zero humanity and no goals beyond perfect order. This is not what the late 2nd edtion/Revised/Onyx Path Technocracy is about. The later Technocracy are agents of change with a goal of a transhumanist Utopia with absolute freedom to all. They are tool users, and they use technology for the masses, but they are people. They have emotions and they will fight tooth and nail to keep the people safe. They may have to do some hard decisions and do questionable choices, but in the long run they are fighting for humanity's betterment... and one day everyone will have supertech that will allow them to truly master the cosmos in a brave new world.<br /> <br /> The Weaver does not seek this wonder and progress. If it were up to the weaver it would stop at any possible level of technology if it was enough to control Reality. The Weaver seeks absolute peace, tranquility and lack of movement.<br /> <br /> On the other hand Changelings are about dreams, wonder and Chaos in the vein of tricksters and whimsical Fae. Wyld is not like that. Wyld is about sprouting cancer out of nowhere, about water flowing backwards, about ice growing from flowers and about horrors that seek to break down reality into a soup that can create endless new vistas.<br /> <br /> It's not a good idea to apply the concepts of Werewolf to any other game, as the cosmology of Werewolf doesn't really play well with others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T03:48:59-07:00","id":517800,"title":"","content":"I tend to look at it differently.<br /> <br /> Not that you are wrong, as I didn't say the Technocracy were necessarily Agents of the Weaver, rather, they are the Mage equivalent of the Weaver ... or, the Technocracy is to Mage as the Weaver is to Garou.<br /> <br /> However, the Weaver would not completely put a halt to the expansion into the cosmos.<br /> <br /> Looking at it through the Technocrat's eyes, the universe is a digital reality. Meaning, it unfolds as it is encountered... but not expanded upon. It is maximized, and given a label.<br /> <br /> Being 1 of the Natural Forces of the Universe itself (relating to the Triat), with its connection to the Umbra (there is a cyber realm), the Weaver is all too familiar with how expansive the Universe is.<br /> <br /> And, as a force, fighting for a unilateral understanding and service to balance, the Technocracy would be the perfect vehicle for the Weaver to utilize in order to get to those far and distant planes, planets, stars and what have yous, if for no better reason than to Web it all together.<br /> <br /> For the Weaver, it would be a wonderful match.<br /> <br /> As for not mixing Werewolf to other games -- I personally feel any chance to cross systems together is a great benefit to every game, as it allows for exposure to those casual cWoD WW fans, who gravitate towards a singular setting, maybe leaning on a secondary genre, who wouldn't generally explore the other denizens without a given excuse.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, the best word of mouth is to put it directly inside someone's comfort zone.<br /> They may just say -- &quot;Oh, I get it now&quot;.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6040,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","user":"Quiet Storm","date":". 05-18-2015, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T04:06:48-07:00","id":517805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=517658#post517658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Besides, it's GENERALLY a bad idea to battle gun-to-claw with the werewolves (<i>for anyone,</i> mage, vampire, fomori or whatever) , but technocrats are crafty, and can surely find a way to even the odds, if they have enough reason to bother. If Pentex can do it, Technocrats will find a way too.<br /> <br /> Much better to point how 3\u00ba edition mages aren't related any more to the Triat (as they used to be). Or how the usual ineptitude with Spirit/DiCi in general and the Middle Umbra in particular makes very hard for technocrats to truly comunicate to the Weaver (even when they're doing Her work, by controlling magick, expanding stasis, etc... That you don't believe in the Weaver doesn't mean that the Weaver doesn't believe in you...).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a very good way of putting it.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T04:10:38-07:00","id":517807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accordiontoplan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=431324#post431324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to the MtSC: Witches and Pagans Pod book....</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow I passed over this comment -- I concur<br /> A Print on Demand; &quot;Witches and Pagans&quot; book<br /> would be well received by fans, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T04:19:19-07:00","id":517809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=517800#post517800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to look at it differently.<br /> <br /> Not that you are wrong, as I didn't say the Technocracy were necessarily Agents of the Weaver, rather, they are the Mage equivalent of the Weaver ... or, the Technocracy is to Mage as the Weaver is to Garou.<br /> <br /> However, the Weaver would not completely put a halt to the expansion into the cosmos.<br /> <br /> Looking at it through the Technocrat's eyes, the universe is a digital reality. Meaning, it unfolds as it is encountered... but not expanded upon. It is maximized, and given a label.<br /> <br /> Being 1 of the Natural Forces of the Universe itself (relating to the Triat), with its connection to the Umbra (there is a cyber realm), the Weaver is all too familiar with how expansive the Universe is.<br /> <br /> And, as a force, fighting for a unilateral understanding and service to balance, the Technocracy would be the perfect vehicle for the Weaver to utilize in order to get to those far and distant planes, planets, stars and what have yous, if for no better reason than to Web it all together.<br /> <br /> For the Weaver, it would be a wonderful match.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's completley missing the point that the Weaver is absolutley insane and the only thing it wants is absolute, constant, fixed and unchanged reality forever more. Weaver is not some misunderstood lord of technology, it's an alien immovable object that seeks the perfection of complete lack of change.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T04:24:14-07:00","id":517812,"title":"","content":"It only seeks the lack of change, after it encounters all that is available to it, then it is drawn in and conformed. Until the entirety of the universe is mapped out, the Weaver can never rest.<br /> <br /> That is exactly the point.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T05:22:14-07:00","id":517877,"title":"","content":"Why would Weaver have to map out the universe? It created it, and knows all about it already. The Universe is its Creation (with a helpful hand from the Wyld and the Weaver). The endgoal of the Weaver is one perfect still image that never, ever changes. This doesn't bode well for the Creative Spirit, Manifest Destiny, Ascension and Reality Warping of Mankind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T05:46:34-07:00","id":517883,"title":"","content":"This. The Weaver and the Technocracy <i>do</i> share vaguely similar roles in their respective games in that both are associated with the principle of Patterns and Stasis. But they each relate to that principle in very different ways: the Weaver is the embodiment of the principles in question; but fr the Technocracy, Stasis is the pitfall that they're most prone to \u2014 it\u2019s not something that they condsider to be a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:12:32-07:00","id":518153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=517702#post517702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The description of the Gift, Jam Technology, specifies that if affects &quot;any devices shaped from fabricated materials such as metal or plastic.&quot; It goes on to mention that it can prevent gunpowder from igniting, so it might work against the drugs (since it's hampering chemical reactions of fabricated objects in this sense, at least if the effect is ongoing), but conditioning isn't within the purview of the Gift at all. For those stalwarts, you would use something like Shadows of the Impergium or Terror of the (ugh) Dire Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm.... using that logic, Jam Technology can get rid of alcohol or even allergic reactions. That's a MASSIVE expansion on the Gift. <br /> <br /> I doubt the intent was anything along those lines. More like &quot;that thing you are holding does not work. However it usually works, that doesn't happen. 'Cause I just told those spirits that make it work to stop doing that.&quot; Particularly when it so very specific about what it works on. You can't make a stone tool stop working. You can't make a wooden tool stop working.<br /> <br /> You couldn't even make a ceramic gun stop working. Are there ceramic guns? There should could be with modern technology., not even hyper-tech. Would the Union issue them to werewolf-killers? Why not? Silver-tipped ceramic fragmentation bullets sound ideal.... (Unless you think that &quot;metal&quot; should include sliver... which undermines the core weakness of the Garou and indicates a substantial increase in their power using this gift, as you can now use it against other Garou's klaives) Particularly in the .50 caliber variety, used by long distance snipers (1 mile sounds about right....).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 05-18-2015, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:30:37-07:00","id":518199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=517800#post517800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for not mixing Werewolf to other games -- I personally feel any chance to cross systems together is a great benefit to every game, as it allows for exposure to those casual cWoD WW fans, who gravitate towards a singular setting, maybe leaning on a secondary genre, who wouldn't generally explore the other denizens without a given excuse.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, the best word of mouth is to put it directly inside someone's comfort zone.<br /> They may just say -- &quot;Oh, I get it now&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there are definitely some fun ideas in combining Werewolf and Mage (or any CWoD games for that matter) there are several very problematic issues in doing so. Werewolf is a game of completely absolute ideology. They are RIGHT. They know the way the universe WORKS. If you don't get their way, then you are deluded and/or wrong. <br /> <br /> Mage is game of perishingly few absolutes. And when you find them, many, if not most, of them are arguable. In Mage, &quot;Being right&quot; is very relative. In a multi-Tradition or multi-Faction group, &quot;right&quot; varies from individual to individual. The universe doesn't work the same for you as it does for me. It doesn't even work the same for all of them THEM (insert whatever you want here - different groups of humans, humans and other supernaturals, different types of supernaturals, groups within specific types of supernatural). You may believe the other person is wrong, but that really has no effect on their ability to do their thing. The universe works in an almost infinite variety of different ways with a loose &quot;democracy of agreement&quot; governing the relative weight of them. <br /> <br /> So you have to try to harmonize those two and that's NOT easy. You can try to handwave it or ignore it, but that will lead to difficulties down the line. Werewolf being the absolutist view, it is the easiest one to cleave to and thereby, make Mage's fundamentals WRONG. They are completely incorrect. It's all about the Weaver/Wyrm/Wild. No way around it. Mage suffers as you try to shoehorn all the variety into boxes that were never meant to hold such things. Alternatively, you can say Mage is correct and Werewolf is correct for only the subset of Reality(-ies) that they interact with. Which sounds good on paper, but it does undermine Werewolf. Now Werewolf's ideology is WRONG. The Wyrm/Weaver/Wild/Gaia are all just their thing. Cool for them. Also a bit limiting don't you think? Technocrats aren't paws or allies of the Weaver. They may see the Weaver as manifestation of a fundamental aspect of the Tellurian in the way the Werewolves see it, but, in the end to the Union, it's another EDE (albeit a weakly-godlike one, at the very least) which it means to be contained/destroyed/used/guarded against. <br /> <br /> Or you can TRY to find a way to harmonize them, but every way I've seen so far ends up with people having to pick one game or the other and going with it. And, unfortunately, end up having to do a disservice to the other game. If you come at things from Werewolf, you will slam down the Triat and MAKE IT MAKE SENSE for Mages by making them pawns of this or that or some combination. Or you pick Mage and go very relativistic and pluralistic and say &quot;Werewolves think X&quot; and then follow from that in how they interact with the various types of Mages. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T10:41:19-07:00","id":518293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=518153#post518153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm.... using that logic, Jam Technology can get rid of alcohol or even allergic reactions. That's a MASSIVE expansion on the Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that alcohol counts. Yeast is doing the heavy lifting there. I don't think that allergic reactions qualify, either, since the only effect stopped is the intended effect of an artifical object or substance and not your immune system going haywire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt the intent was anything along those lines. More like &quot;that thing you are holding does not work. However it usually works, that doesn't happen. 'Cause I just told those spirits that make it work to stop doing that.&quot; Particularly when it so very specific about what it works on. You can't make a stone tool stop working. You can't make a wooden tool stop working. </div> </div> </div>Gunpowder failing to ignite was an example in the Gift, as was the description &quot;the simplest shaped objects refuse to function&quot;. Hence, you can totally make stone tools stop working. Blocking a knife is difficulty 9, and it won't cut for the admittedly limited duration of the Gift, whether it was forged, carved or knapped. Being shaped by human hands alters the material spiritually. See also, the similar Gift Jam Weapon, which specifically works only on offensive devices, but doesn't allow anything short of a rock snatched from the ground or a fallen tree branch past its watch, and has a much longer range. It wouldn't block drugs that have yet to take effect or require a constant presence, though, unless they were used as weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You couldn't even make a ceramic gun stop working. Are there ceramic guns? There should could be with modern technology., not even hyper-tech. Would the Union issue them to werewolf-killers? Why not? Silver-tipped ceramic fragmentation bullets sound ideal.... (Unless you think that &quot;metal&quot; should include sliver... which undermines the core weakness of the Garou and indicates a substantial increase in their power using this gift, as you can now use it against other Garou's klaives) Particularly in the .50 caliber variety, used by long distance snipers (1 mile sounds about right....). </div> </div> </div>All those are doable; the only problem is the limited range and time of the Gift (a few turns, and only within about running distance). In the sniper case, it'd probably be more useful to use Gremlins or Control Simple Machine. The former can even brick devices permanently, if you roll well enough.<br /> <br /> I'm seriously not understanding why you'd think that ceramics somehow wouldn't fall under the purview of Jam Technology, though. The material that they'd be created from would be incredibly sophisticated in terms of the production process. That's helluva fabricated. Also, silver in .50 BMG? It wouldn't be effective at that range. Silver has monumentally shitty ballistics. The round would fly apart long before it managed to reach the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:04:49-07:00","id":518311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Weaver and the Technocracy <i>do</i> share vaguely similar roles in their respective games in that both are associated with the principle of Patterns and Stasis. But they each relate to that principle in very different ways: the Weaver is the embodiment of the principles in question; but fr the Technocracy, Stasis is the pitfall that they're most prone to...</div> </div> </div> </div>While I totaly agree on that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it\u2019s not something that they condsider to be a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't entirely agree with this. The 1\u00ba and most important Principle of Damian, the law of technocracy, clearly states that stasis it's good, that it has to be enforced through all the universe.<br /> <br /> Of course, saner technocrats interpret this not as too literally bring the universe to a halt, but to &quot;fix&quot; it permanently into a sane, healthy, place. Technocrats would oppose to the Weaver, should they know it's true goal. But they don't, and they &quot;bring stasis&quot; agenda furthers the agenda of the Weaver.<br /> <br /> Of course, while tech-heads might be &quot;useful&quot; to the Weaver for now, eventually they will have to be destroyed/calcified too, as all magick comes from the principle of dynamism, and technocratic ideals aren't less of a force of change (though it's a form of controlled change). Then again, the same can be said of all life...<br /> <br /> I don't see how any of this diminishes the potential of a crossover technocracy/weaver. Only for those that want to see Technocracy as a force of undeniable good can be offended by the fact that its workings may relate (directly, but unknown to them) to a cosmic force that want's to calcify the universe. <hr />EDIT:<br /> <br /> As for Mage line, I would like a &quot;Book of Classic Ways&quot; (similar to Spirit Ways) that depicts the magick of the Order of Hermes, Celestial Chorus (and Order of Reason Freemasons), with new rules and tweaks for things like true names, relationship with angels and demons and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-18-2015, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T12:13:15-07:00","id":518365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=518293#post518293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that alcohol counts. Yeast is doing the heavy lifting there. I don't think that allergic reactions qualify, either, since the only effect stopped is the intended effect of an artifical object or substance and not your immune system going haywire.because<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Gunpowder failing to ignite was an example in the Gift, as was the description &quot;the simplest shaped objects refuse to function&quot;. Hence, you can totally make stone tools stop working. Blocking a knife is difficulty 9, and it won't cut for the admittedly limited duration of the Gift, whether it was forged, carved or knapped. Being shaped by human hands alters the material spiritually. See also, the similar Gift Jam Weapon, which specifically works only on offensive devices, but doesn't allow anything short of a rock snatched from the ground or a fallen tree branch past its watch, and has a much longer range. It wouldn't block drugs that have yet to take effect or require a constant presence, though, unless they were used as weapons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All those are doable; the only problem is the limited range and time of the Gift (a few turns, and only within about running distance). In the sniper case, it'd probably be more useful to use Gremlins or Control Simple Machine. The former can even brick devices permanently, if you roll well enough.<br /> <br /> I'm seriously not understanding why you'd think that ceramics somehow wouldn't fall under the purview of Jam Technology, though. The material that they'd be created from would be incredibly sophisticated in terms of the production process. That's helluva fabricated. Also, silver in .50 BMG? It wouldn't be effective at that range. Silver has monumentally shitty ballistics. The round would fly apart long before it managed to reach the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you are taking these Gifts and using them far, far, far outside the original intent. Like I said, the intent was obviously &quot;weapon not work&quot;. It wasn't based in the esoterics of how technology makes anything work. The gunpowder isn't important. It's the fact it's a gun. A gun is a machine. A gun is a weapon. The power works on them for that reason. It does not work on the gunpowder specifically. Nor does it work on the kinetic energy of pulling the trigger. Nor does it work on the kinetic energy produced by the expanding gas of the explosion that propels the bullet out of the barrel of the gun. Nor does it apply to the reactive forces that allow for the barrel to contain the explosion or to those that allow the trigger to work. The Gift isn't about the mechanics and science of how guns work. It's about the essence &quot;gun-ness&quot;. That's how spirits work. Meaning, metaphor, essence, not based on a positivist reductionism of the processes involved. Jam Technology will work on a car as well, but not it's stopping the process of internal combustion from occurring or the principles of kinetics that allow wheels to turn from occurring, but because it &quot;jams&quot; the &quot;technology&quot; of the engine. It tells the car spirit not to go. As a result, each of those things don't happen, but that's not the cause, it's the effect.<br /> <br /> Your reasoning on alcohol not working doesn't follow from what you've said. Unless it's alcohol from eating rotten fruit fallen from a wild tree, it's definitely been worked over heavily by humans. If you see Jam Technology as taking out chemical reactions in the brain b/c they are &quot;unnatural&quot;, &quot;made&quot; things, alcohol definitely qualifies. The yeast doesn't do any of the lifting except at the behest of its human overloads. Also all the OTHER processes that go into making wine or beer. Much less hard alcohol. Alcohol might be more processed than cocaine or heroin (depending on the purity). If Jam Technology works on chemicals taken to reduce susceptibility to any of the magical &quot;Don't see me&quot; powers, then it would definitely have a similar effect on alcohol, coffee or laudanum. Likewise allergic reactions to pollen or dander might be problematic under this definition, unless, say the plant or animal in question was domesticated (so maybe not so much on cat dander?). It would definitely apply to an allergic reaction to anything processed. Latex allergy? Sure! Allergy to penicillin? Done!<br /> <br /> If you start expanding the powers in this way, you've made simple direct Gifts massively overpowering and have really undermined much of the animistic feel of Werewolf. It's become an exercise in &quot;how much science can I spiel out to BS the ST into allowing me to use this Gift way past it's envelope.&quot; Which is really more of a Mage thing....<br /> <br /> Also, not a silver bullet, a ceramic bullet with a lot of silver in it, flechette-style or something even cooler. I'm sure Technocracy ballistic science is amazing. No worries making a bullet that will have enough silver but still be ballistic (or just get someone with Matter 4 to make some ceramic that is also pure silver, or pure silver that can be made into decent bullets). But, you're dead right. Such a bullet is definitely very very technologically processed. You'd need to have a cool-ass scope to know when there was some kind of &quot;anti-tech&quot; field up... hold your action... then &lt;pft&gt; (I'm assuming they just threw in silencing, b/c why not?) Werewolf head explodes with usoakable Agg damage! Make sure to pick the one generating the field as Target 1. Then take the rest out according to threat assessment ranking....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 05-18-2015, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T13:23:03-07:00","id":518417,"title":"","content":"This <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocrats would oppose the Weaver, should they know its true goal</div> </div> </div> </div>and this <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">technocratic ideals aren't less of a force for change</div> </div> </div> </div>are the sorts of things I was referring to when I said that technocrats consider falling into the trap of too much Stasis to be a bad thing. Even the second edition\u2019s Technocracy reacts poorly to much of what the Weaver is doing. That\u2019s not portraying them as a force for undeniable good; that\u2019s portraying them as not being total nitwits and rubes. They\u2019re dangerous and In many ways harmful; it\u2019s just that much of the harm they do has nothing to do with Stasis as the Weaver embodies it. <br /> <br /> That said: if you <i>want</i> to portray them as agents of the Weaver, you can do so without <i>too</i> much trouble. Prior to the recent revised Convention Books, the Conventions took their orders from Control<sup>*</sup>; and the game has made a point not to provide a definitive answer as to what Control is. If you want to rule that, for the purpose of Werewolf/Mage crossover games, Control is the Weaver (or has been coopted by the Weaver), go for it! But I absolutely would <i>not</i> want a W20 Book of the Weaver to unequivocally state that this is absolutely the case. Heck, even if it <i>is</i> the case, it only means that the Technocracy was under the Weaver\u2019s influence for part of their history: as near as I can tell, Control is something that only became a force within the Conventions for less than a century: it <i>may</i> have been in place as early as the late 1890s, when the more oppressive elements of the Union took over; and according to the recent Convention Books, it lost its hold in the late 1990s with the rise of the Avatar Storm. <br /> <br /> Ironically, the big problem concerning Werewolf/Mage crossovers involves a sort of inversion of the usual criticism leveled against Mage fans, namely the claim that they try to shoehorn everything into Mage\u2019s cosmology. In the case of Werewolf, the problems arise when you try to shoehorn everything into <i>Werewolf</i>'s cosmology. Doing so essentially says several things: first, Spirit is the most important of the Spheres, because everything is ultimately about the Umbra and its inhabitants. Second, mages only matter in terms of which Umbral factions they\u2019re aligned with (knowingly or unknowingly), as 1the central premise of humanism in Mage is at direct odds with the central importance of spiritualism in Werewolf: in Werewolf, humans are presented as pawns of the various Umbral factions: technology was one of the Weaver's gifts to humanity; creativity and imagination are only possible because of the Wyld; and the Wyrm is ultimately responsible for anything that degrades, corrupts, or pollutes. But in Mage, humans are the captains of their own destinies, whether they know it or not; and mages in particular are those humans who know it. Forcing Werewolf\u2019s perspective onto Mage undermines that central premise. <br /> <br /> That\u2019s not to say that crossovers can\u2019t be made to work; but there should at least be an option of presenting the Triat as \u201cmerely\u201d the Middle Umbra\u2019s expression of the triune principles of the Metaphysics of Magic. A Werewolf book should not be defining core truths of Mage, or Changeling, or any other gameline. There should be Technocrats who <i>don\u2019t</i> serve the Weaver but are at most allies of convenience and quite possibly its rivals, just as the Nephandi who serve the Wyrm are but one faction of several among the Fallen. <br /> <br /> <hr />* In the Revised Convention Book, the premise is that the Conventions were cut off from Control by the Avatar Storm, and are now free agents \u2014 save only for those who were trapped in the Umbra by the Storm and eventually Discorporated, turning into what the Void Engineers call Threat Null.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T13:44:44-07:00","id":518427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...That said: if you <i>want</i> to portray them as agents of the Weaver... </div> </div> </div>No I never say that, what I implied it's that, in a crossover, the work of the Technocracy as agents of stability and order benefits the plans of the Weaver.<br /> <br /> Not all weaverish stuff it's bad, even some Werewolves (who know the kind of harm that the Weaver has done) think that there's more good than bad in the Weaver. Technocrats hardly know anything about the Weaver (Middle Umbra it's not their forte), they can't know that the stability that they bring, while holding off many of the evils of oWoD, it's also fortifying the position of yet another peril to the humanity, much less understand it's nature.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Take, for instance, the position of Technocrats (even void engineers) about the Gauntlet. Do they want to weaken it?. Voiders would benefit, but for the good of mankind, they won't. Too bad that there's another force that's interested in strengthening the Gauntlet with a less humanistic goal in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your reasoning on alcohol not working doesn't follow from what you've said. Unless it's alcohol from eating rotten fruit fallen from a wild tree, it's definitely been worked over heavily by humans. If you see Jam Technology as taking out chemical reactions in the brain b/c they are &quot;unnatural&quot;, &quot;made&quot; things, alcohol definitely qualifies. The yeast doesn't do any of the lifting except at the behest of its human overloads. Also all the OTHER processes that go into making wine or beer. Much less hard alcohol. Alcohol might be more processed than cocaine or heroin (depending on the purity). If Jam Technology works on chemicals taken to reduce susceptibility to any of the magical &quot;Don't see me&quot; powers, then it would definitely have a similar effect on alcohol, coffee or laudanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the effects of chemicals should not be affected by Jam Technology (otherwise, it will replace &quot;Resist Toxin&quot; against any non natural chemical, among other thousand uses). Albeit a &quot;dispenser&quot; such as a vaccine might.<br /> <br /> Can we interpret the rest as &quot;tech-guys are clever and dangerous, they can be good antagonist&quot;, instead of Mage vs Garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-18-2015, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T13:58:42-07:00","id":518429,"title":"","content":"I'd like:<br /> - A Changeling book about the Fae outside Concordia: South America, Africa, Asia, Europe, Oceania.<br /> - A KotE about the Kuei-Jin outside Asia.<br /> -A Changeling translation guide.<br /> -A H:tR version of Mortal Remains.<br /> -A Changeling book on the Interregnum.<br /> -A Werewolf book on the politics of the Garou Nation.<br /> -A Changeling book on Changeling/Dreamer interactions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:20:58-07:00","id":518504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=518427#post518427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I never say that, what I implied it's that, in a crossover, the work of the Technocracy as agents of stability and order benefits the plans of the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes. Often, even. But not always. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all weaverish stuff it's bad, even some Werewolves (who know the kind of harm that the Weaver has done) think that there's more good than bad in the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course; I've never claimed otherwise. This isn\u2019t about \u201cTechnocracy good; Weaver bad\u201d; it\u2019s about \u201cTechnocracy and Weaver don\u2019t always align\u201d. Sometimes they do; often, even. But not always.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=518429#post518429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like:<br /> - A Changeling book about the Fae outside Concordia: South America, Africa, Asia, Europe, Oceania.<br /> - A KotE about the Kuei-Jin outside Asia.<br /> -A Changeling translation guide.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=518429#post518429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-A H:tR version of Mortal Remains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's called <b>Hunter: Urban Legends</b>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=518429#post518429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-A Changeling book on the Interregnum.<br /> -A Werewolf book on the politics of the Garou Nation.<br /> -A Changeling book on Changeling/Dreamer interactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>These all sound good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T16:29:42-07:00","id":518567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=518365#post518365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that you are taking these Gifts and using them far, far, far outside the original intent. Like I said, the intent was obviously &quot;weapon not work&quot;. It wasn't based in the esoterics of how technology makes anything work. The gunpowder isn't important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally, from the text of the Gift, it says that it won't ignite. It deigns to deliver this information with word count as an example malfunction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's the fact it's a gun. A gun is a machine. A gun is a weapon. The power works on them for that reason. It does not work on the gunpowder specifically. Nor does it work on the kinetic energy of pulling the trigger. Nor does it work on the kinetic energy produced by the expanding gas of the explosion that propels the bullet out of the barrel of the gun. Nor does it apply to the reactive forces that allow for the barrel to contain the explosion or to those that allow the trigger to work. The Gift isn't about the mechanics and science of how guns work. </div> </div> </div>The description begs to differ, since different degrees of sophistication make it easier for the Gift to work. Gunpowder and thus chemicals must be at one of those break points, or else they wouldn't have deigned to mention that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's about the essence &quot;gun-ness&quot;. That's how spirits work. Meaning, metaphor, essence, not based on a positivist reductionism of the processes involved. Jam Technology will work on a car as well, but not it's stopping the process of internal combustion from occurring or the principles of kinetics that allow wheels to turn from occurring, but because it &quot;jams&quot; the &quot;technology&quot; of the engine. It tells the car spirit not to go. As a result, each of those things don't happen, but that's not the cause, it's the effect. </div> </div> </div>It overwhelms the technological workings with stasis or chaos. Again, from the text of the Gift, that is how it works. You're probably thinking of Jam Weapon, a different, lower-ranked Gift that works on the intent of weaponry. It's the only Gift that really bothers with it, and has different mechanics to reflect this (opposed Willpower roll with weapon users instead of rolling against inversely correlated tech sophistication difficulty).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your reasoning on alcohol not working doesn't follow from what you've said. Unless it's alcohol from eating rotten fruit fallen from a wild tree, it's definitely been worked over heavily by humans. If you see Jam Technology as taking out chemical reactions in the brain b/c they are &quot;unnatural&quot;, &quot;made&quot; things, alcohol definitely qualifies. The yeast doesn't do any of the lifting except at the behest of its human overloads. </div> </div> </div>Even if it did fall under the envelope, JT would only prevent you from getting drunk for a few seconds. I'm not sure why you're up in arms about the two turns per success reprieve on alcohol absorption or Derelex-Lupus nullification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also all the OTHER processes that go into making wine or beer. Much less hard alcohol. Alcohol might be more processed than cocaine or heroin (depending on the purity). If Jam Technology works on chemicals taken to reduce susceptibility to any of the magical &quot;Don't see me&quot; powers, then it would definitely have a similar effect on alcohol, coffee or laudanum. Likewise allergic reactions to pollen or dander might be problematic under this definition, unless, say the plant or animal in question was domesticated (so maybe not so much on cat dander?). It would definitely apply to an allergic reaction to anything processed. Latex allergy? Sure! Allergy to penicillin? Done! </div> </div> </div>Don't blame me. The text is what says that propellants refuse to explode, most likely be overwhelming it with a spiritual force of stasis, again, from the description of the Gift. It probably didn't intend on allergic reactions seeing as how the allergic reaction isn't part of the effect that pouring in Weaver or Wyld energy would stop. It's there and sits inert with regard to its intended function for a few moments, but the immune reaction is still going to go through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you start expanding the powers in this way, you've made simple direct Gifts massively overpowering and have really undermined much of the animistic feel of Werewolf. It's become an exercise in &quot;how much science can I spiel out to BS the ST into allowing me to use this Gift way past it's envelope.&quot; Which is really more of a Mage thing.. </div> </div> </div>Gremlins (the spirits, not the Gift) like their specifics. Goes with the territory of loving how shit breaks, I suppose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, not a silver bullet, a ceramic bullet with a lot of silver in it, flechette-style or something even cooler. I'm sure Technocracy ballistic science is amazing. No worries making a bullet that will have enough silver but still be ballistic (or just get someone with Matter 4 to make some ceramic that is also pure silver, or pure silver that can be made into decent bullets). But, you're dead right. Such a bullet is definitely very very technologically processed. You'd need to have a cool-ass scope to know when there was some kind of &quot;anti-tech&quot; field up... hold your action... then &lt;pft&gt; (I'm assuming they just threw in silencing, b/c why not?) Werewolf head explodes with usoakable Agg damage! Make sure to pick the one generating the field as Target 1. Then take the rest out according to threat assessment ranking.... </div> </div> </div>There are loads of questions with that scenario that make it not worth considering, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:01:15-07:00","id":519698,"title":"","content":"Tables won't work. How does that manifest? The stuff falls through to the ground? The table falls apart? <br /> Shoes won't work. Are you stuck to the ground? Do they fall apart?<br /> Glasses won't work. I mean the kind that hold liquid. Plus the other ones. Sucks to be near-sighted. Plus all the liquids are now puddles? <br /> Clothes don't work. So they fly off an leave you naked? They stop protecting you from the environment? Like they become transparent to cold? The no longer indicate your social status? Do they fall apart into natural threads? What happens if it's rayon? Does it mean kevlar doesn't stop bullets anymore? <br /> Food doesn't work. So do your cells stop processing materials not from processed food? So heavy energy use cells, like muscle tissue, don't work? So you can use Jam Technology on someone who has imbibed an energy drink to reduce them to a wreck, writhing with horrible cramps? (This one is DEFINITELY in line with your original example)<br /> Fire doesn't work. <br /> Doors don't work<br /> Houses don't work.<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Consider those scenarios. <br /> <br /> For a Gift meant to make cars stop, computers just sit there with blank screens, phones not make calls (I'd rate smartphones with computers) and guns not fire it seems really really really powerful using this interpretation. It's a complete Technocracy/technomancer destroyer. (Low Diff on all their stuff). It also takes out pretty much any other Mage or other human or other supernatural without claws and teeth. Using this definition almost all magic is void ab initio, as it involves some use of something processed by humans at some point. Does it work on Changeling chimerical tech? They are all in human vessels after all....<br /> <br /> Gremlins tearing through people's brains and muscles and causing the chemicals to &quot;fall apart&quot; or &quot;break&quot; (with TONS of nasty side effects) does not seem to fall within the intent of the Gift. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T11:03:36-07:00","id":519777,"title":"","content":"I use Jam Technology in a prison cell door-should it open (as its intended function it's to keep people in)?, or should it become impossible to open (as the door mechanism won't move)?.<br /> <br /> It's too complicated. I would make it work against mechanisms (door won't open), electronics, and chemicals that are important to the functioning of technological devices. So, gasoline will still be flammable, but won't burn to move a motor. It will never affect a chemical that has already been ingested (as a matter of principles, it should never act so directly on a living organism. Though it will affect electromechanic stuff inside the body, like an implanted chip)<br /> <br /> Someone think that interpretation it's flawed somehow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:41:29-07:00","id":519888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=519777#post519777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use Jam Technology in a prison cell door-should it open (as its intended function it's to keep people in)?, or should it become impossible to open (as the door mechanism won't move)?.</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't lock, but that would require dialing things up to &quot;knife&quot; level on JT and you wouldn't have much time to dash to the door and manually open it before it was spiritually &quot;closed&quot; again. Open Seal and Control Simple Machine would be far simpler and more efficient for that task, unless, in the former case, the Gauntlet was really high.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's too complicated. I would make it work against mechanisms (door won't open), electronics, and chemicals that are important to the functioning of technological devices. So, gasoline will still be flammable, but won't burn to move a motor. It will never affect a chemical that has already been ingested (as a matter of principles, it should never act so directly on a living organism. Though it will affect electromechanic stuff inside the body, like an implanted chip) </div> </div> </div>A better standard for the body might be anything that wouldn't typically be found in the body. So it can't normally adversely affect anyone, but it can, say, temporarily disable the latent IV agents used in various forms of metamorphosis inhibitor, or make anyone using oxygenated fluorocarbons to be in a place that humans wouldn't normally be able to be found have a very dicey moment (but that wouldn't be very different from disabling a SCUBA system while underwater and robbing a wetsuit or drysuit of its ability to insulate a diver, for all of the scant few seconds you'll make someone hold their breath).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T13:45:28-07:00","id":519979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=518504#post518504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe it's called [b]Hunter: Urban Legends</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! *crosses off list*.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T14:35:07-07:00","id":520009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=519888#post519888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They wouldn't lock, but that would require dialing things up to &quot;knife&quot; level on JT and you wouldn't have much time to dash to the door and manually open it before it was spiritually &quot;closed&quot; again. Open Seal and Control Simple Machine would be far simpler and more efficient for that task, unless, in the former case, the Gauntlet was really high.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A better standard for the body might be anything that wouldn't typically be found in the body. So it can't normally adversely affect anyone, but it can, say, temporarily disable the latent IV agents used in various forms of metamorphosis inhibitor, or make anyone using oxygenated fluorocarbons to be in a place that humans wouldn't normally be able to be found have a very dicey moment (but that wouldn't be very different from disabling a SCUBA system while underwater and robbing a wetsuit or drysuit of its ability to insulate a diver, for all of the scant few seconds you'll make someone hold their breath).</div> </div> </div> </div>So opiates are immune to the Gift. And, if that energy is from an energy drink or fast food, you will collapse to the ground screaming as your muscles seize up. Powerful, powerful Gift. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd go for the door thing, but, if it's in someone's body, I think it should be beyond the power of the Gift and that certainly fits within the reading, the general spirit of Werewolf and the way powers scale as well. Summoning up Gremlins and having them ravage people internally sounds like it is a serious bad ass thing to do, but it's NOT a thing covered by Jam Technology. If a wolf ( or Red Talon) eats the poppies, he goes loopy too. If he eats the cocoa leaves he gets all frenetic. If he eats heroin or cocaine (or drinks coffee or eats tobacco) the same things should happen and THIS Gift shouldn't mess with it. I can easily see another Gift like Sober Up or something that does exactly what you are saying. It &quot;jams&quot; internal chemical tech. With some nice side effects like doing B damage to people who eat too much junk food, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T18:26:20-07:00","id":530476,"title":"","content":"After seeing how much of the metaplot was presented in M20 through sidebars and how inclusive of the older material it was, the book I want is a V20 2.0 that offers all these metaplot options back and suggests the older books to look at for more information like M20 did. It's amazing, and also doesn't seem scarred to include Revised era material, too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:05:02-07:00","id":884244,"title":"","content":"Technocracy: Cold War. : from the Kennedy Assassination to watergate and beyond.<br /> A setting book for Ancient Rome:vampire + Wraith + Werewolf.<br /> Changeling: maybe a short adventure set on the Flower Power Era.<br /> World of Darkness: Age of the Plague: basically a setting book set during the Black Plague (for different settings)-<br /> World of Darkness: Necropolis Earth: basically, the biggest necropolis and disasters of the world. Chernobyl , Fukushima, etc..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:56:32-07:00","id":884280,"title":"","content":"Guide to Disparate: It would be like the guides to the Traditions and the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T21:11:47-07:00","id":884339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future#post363273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Book of Antiquity: I don\u2019t know what should be the form, just a sourcebook or a stand-alone as DA, but I would really loved to have some details Of Rome, Sparte, Carthage and stuff like that. Background, new rules and that kind of things. It would make a great KS too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be sweet. Heck maybe history book further in the past from 'dark ages'.. like in the Roman era..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=363734#post363734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtO20: Viva La Revolucion (A Wraith book for South America and the Revoluciones and Dictatorships)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice idea. Heck i wouldn't mind seeing MORE for south america.. The only real book i see for down there is rage across the Amazon..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369450#post369450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Human Guide to The World of Darkness: A small one shot detailing HOW IS the World of Darkness from a completely HUMAN point of view, what products can you buy from Pentex, what TV shows are people watching and such. i dont imagine it longer than 15 pages with some art involving people doing normal things (and maybe a supernatural in the background with out being noticed)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, a much larger book on just good old fashioned mortals would be nice to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369450#post369450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Seas of Blood: a one shot book for rules on Ship battles</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Air power and sea power seem to be the 2 most overlooked aspects of all the WoD games from my POV..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369450#post369450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wraith The Oblivion: Massacres.: a book set on the Nephwracks born from &quot;Going Postal.&quot;, Haunting on High Schools and public massacres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am with Atamajikki, in that this would be in poor taste. How ever something from say the time frame of the Korean-Vietnam era would be ok IMO..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369450#post369450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A One shot for Wraith: Ashes And Cinder: a Book for wriaths of Pompei.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why just wraith? IMO that might be a good crossover setting book..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369450#post369450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worlds of Darkness: What if--<br /> - Humanity Always knew about the supernatural and this was common to see. (Imagine Law and Order: Special Supernatural Unit, or to have an official Kindread President)</div> </div> </div> </div>With how popular those sorts of shows (Cop and supernatural ones) are these days, that might be a good idea..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=376909#post376909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hunter: As far as I know, we have Demon Hunter X and Strike Team Zero, though I wonder about something. Are there any Imbued in Asia and if so what do they do for their Hunts? Are there any new Creeds that developed in the Middle Kingdom? I think there should be a Lotus book about Reckoning-type Hunters in Asia and how they Hunt there, What does everyone think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like to see that. Especially to see how the imbued would SEE the Shi or the members of Strike team zero..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=369450#post369450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20: How i Met your Garou.: Another rapid fire book involving Family, how do garous understand their Human family. how do you ask your biological mother &quot;Ermm..why am i a werewolf?&quot;. touching subjects as family both inside and outside the caern (see it as garou kin and also as human kin). some examples (mainly using the family from Teen Wolf as an example) as well rules for reproduction between garous and kinfolks, how to make a human a kinfolk. rituals of pregnancy and garou marriage or partnership, how do tribes see this and how do garou families works (as well other changing breeds).</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who's always loved Fera Kinfolk, i would love that sort of book..<br /> <br /> Long post so will split into another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T21:23:46-07:00","id":884349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=471362#post471362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh..Hunter20 (or hunter 15)<br /> a dream to come, honestly what i would love its if they mention how the hunters and hunter net has evolved. the usage of Twitter and such).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering if someone was going to hit on that. With how social media in the real world has exploded wildly, how does it affect the supers..<br /> Heck maybe just a WoD20 book showing what its impact Has been (or could be) to each super, and their mortal brethren (ghouls/kinfolk etc)..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=493708#post493708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that <b>Psychics </b>could get their own book, or at least a dedicated section of the book, as well as a segment on where the two meet. (An example being Via Ignis from the old Inquisition book, which seems to be a Psychic power amongst their rituals. Other possibilities would be a Shapeshifter developing Biocontrol or Animal Psi, or a Pyrokenetic learning Hellfire to better control his abilities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Heck a guide to those with various Numina, and new rules FOR their use (including maybe some playable templates) would be nice.. Maybe even a section in there, on how each other supernatural group see's those. Much like the tribe/clan books had a little area showing what other tribes/clans felt about that group..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=471362#post471362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">World of Darkness: Age of the Plague: basically a setting book set during the Black Plague (for different settings)-</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck we could also do one updated to say the SARS and Bird flu issues, along with Ebola and other nasty diseases..<br /> <br /> And on that line, what about a guide book to natural disasters both historical and imagined.. What would say the world look like if the Ring of fire errupted? Or if the Big one hit the San Andreas fault line...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:21:27-07:00","id":884385,"title":"","content":"Im currently working on two projects sometimes.<br /> Profilers: A Guide to Disturbed Individuals. Which is pretty much my translation from Slashers to WoD but AVOIDING ALL THE SUPERNATURAL INFLUENCE. More than a &quot;You can play as a Serial Killer.&quot; im keeping it as a &quot;What would a Serial Killer in the WoD Do.&quot;<br /> <br /> and im also (slowly but steadily) working on the Humans for WoD. but like i said its more like a What TV Shows do people watch, what products can you buy and such. Not trying to marry to the canon or anything.<br /> <br /> now, IF anyone wishes to do the small Wraith Viva La Revolucion, Do let me know and i can write down about my country <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:01:24-07:00","id":886849,"title":"","content":"<b>Haunts II: </b>A collection of real life and fictional and haunts and disaster sites like the Armstrong Air and Space Museum (which is said to be one of the most haunted), the site of the Amagasaki rail crash, etc.<br /> <b>Book of Kingdoms:</b> A collection on the other kingdoms in W:tO: Swar, Mirrorlands, Seas That Knows No Sun, Dark Kingdom of Ivory, etc. (I always found Swar to be quite interesting.)<br /> <b>Angel: The Revelation:</b> Kidding. Kidding. (Though I can always hope.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 05-11-2016, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:52:18-07:00","id":888578,"title":"","content":"I'd offer up my house if it meant getting a Hunter the Reckoning 20th(or 15th) anniversary edition. <br /> <br /> And I have a pretty nice house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:37:35-07:00","id":889192,"title":"","content":"Please let us have Demon: the Fallen 15th Anniversary Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T11:50:06-07:00","id":890053,"title":"","content":"I would like to find more mages' crafts, and sourcebooks about the other changelings out from Ch20.<br /> <br /> The return of &quot;Morpheus&quot;, &quot;Kindred of the East&quot;, Hunter: the reckoning, Dark Age: Inquisition. (maybe also Dark Age: Mage), Mummy: Resurection and Demon the Fallen.<br /> <br /> * A crossover Kult: lost divinity and WoD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T17:23:36-07:00","id":890876,"title":"","content":"Something I'd like to see is a general book for all splats(or maybe one for each) that's look at what each one would look like if the masquerade,veil,ect. suddenly stopped or never existed in the first place. some books like NWOD mirrors have touched on it but i'd love a dedicated book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T02:05:56-07:00","id":893157,"title":"","content":"Would like mage in the Asia, and another for Russia maybe.<br /> <br /> Oh and something that covered more dark staff in Mage. You know, a peek on the skeletons mages keep. Dead Magic is good, but too short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 05-18-2016, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T02:07:57-07:00","id":893159,"title":"","content":"Honestly I would just be happy if they got cracking on the books already in the pipe. (Looking at you M20 books)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T02:10:25-07:00","id":893160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=890876#post890876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'd like to see is a general book for all splats(or maybe one for each) that's look at what each one would look like if the masquerade,veil,ect. suddenly stopped or never existed in the first place. some books like NWOD mirrors have touched on it but i'd love a dedicated book</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah, I would love to too. I think the way it had been addressed in Beast is better then assumed informational vacoom that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T00:11:44-07:00","id":894592,"title":"","content":"One of the things I regret not ever getting the opportunity to get my hands on was the <b>Rage Across Africa / Ahadi </b>sourcebook that was being thrown around when the lines got the can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:51:39-07:00","id":896762,"title":"","content":"I want those books for the Nephandi:<br /> Sect Book: K'llashaa<br /> Sect Book: Infernal<br /> Sect Book: Malfean<br /> Sect Book: Technepandi<br /> Sect Book: the Lost (for all the other Nephandi, Nephandic Sects, and Mages blurring the lines)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-28-2017, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T00:53:03-07:00","id":898736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=896762#post896762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want those books for the Nephandi:<br /> Sect Book: K'llashaa<br /> Sect Book: Infernal<br /> Sect Book: Malfean<br /> Sect Book: Technepandi<br /> Sect Book: the Damned and the Lost (for all the other Nephandi, Nephandic Sects, and Mages blurring the lines)</div> </div> </div> </div>600 pages for the Nephandi is really pushing it... You really don't have that much to say about all of them. Even the Book of Madness and Infernalism: The Path of Screams were treading the same ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T18:14:51-07:00","id":902404,"title":"","content":"Phil was talking about a Book of the Fallen during the M20 Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">