th.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T08:38:11-07:00","id":905669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=905086#post905086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And with how there were a lot more open areas to inter in without getting messed with, gangrel should have it easiest..</div> </div> </div> </div>They are the only one I can see moving West, cause they are not bound to a city as much as every clan is. But I'm taking in account all the clans, not just Gangrels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T09:40:13-07:00","id":905716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=905669#post905669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are the only one I can see moving West, cause they are not bound to a city as much as every clan is. But I'm taking in account all the clans, not just Gangrels.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can go a lot of places by steamboat. Vampires crossed the Atlantic Ocean to settle in the New World. I'm betting that there are several creative tried-and-true situations to deal with travel that don't involve Earth Meld. There are definitely records of wagon trains that actually carried coffins filled with dead folks with them (which freaked out the tribes they encountered). It wouldn't be too hard to put a concealed &quot;smuggler&quot; space in a Condestoga wagon. And, once a vampire arrives at a destination, they're in pretty much the same situation they would be anywhere else that was relatively thinly populated (which was a lot of places vampires, including but not limited to Gangrel, did just fine in back in the day...)<br /> <br /> I didn't find it too difficult to work up a fast and dirty version of Mage for the Wild West when the characters in one game ended up going back in time. They got a couple of handouts describing the differences and ended up stumbling across a lot of others I planned out and extrapolated out on the fly. I did a similar work up for my own purposes of the vampire, werewolf and wraith populations of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:08:49-07:00","id":905937,"title":"","content":"Sweet.. Though to me, one of the bigger issues with the whole moving west, is the lessening of sufficient herd sizes to cope with more than just 2-3 vampires per west town..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T17:39:49-07:00","id":906074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=905937#post905937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sweet.. Though to me, one of the bigger issues with the whole moving west, is the lessening of sufficient herd sizes to cope with more than just 2-3 vampires per west town..</div> </div> </div> </div>Things would probably be more like the Dark Ages as far as vamp to vessel ratio. Plus... Sabbat packs. And lots of animals to eat. Enough even to make up for the fact that they are thin gruel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.