er\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T19:31:39-07:00","id":1081239,"title":"","content":"For Vampire:<br /> <b>Guide to the Sabbat</b><br /> Really needs an overhaul. Near Dark was scary for it's time, but redneck vampire rampage could use some rethinking today.<br /> <b>Blood Magic 2</b><br /> Instead of details on the magic itself, instead make this an 'adventure' book. The main clans that use various forms of Blood Magic competing for a prize that promises to increase their powers. (or at least the powers of their elders.) Basically, Giovanni, vs Tremere, vs Old Clan Tsimisce, with a scattering of Settites and Assamites.<br /> <br /> For Werewolf:<br /> <b>Rage Across</b>... focusing on the Ahadi. It's rise, and the challenges it faces.<br /> This was one that sounded like it was picking up steam before the change over to the new WoD.<br /> While most of the Breedbooks were pretty awesome,<br /> <b>Nuwisha </b>and <b>Bastet </b>are both showing their age.<br /> Nuwisha was so heavily reliant on other books, at times it seems like 'the Ragabash tribe with no Rage'<br /> Bastet just has some goofy things that need to be addressed, and possibly the <b>Ajaba </b>spun into their own Breedbook.<br /> (Why do the Swara get to step sideways early due to 'ties with the land', while the Pumonca make a much bigger deal about that? Why does the Kahn yava mention their ties with the Sun, when the Simba are the 'Lords of Sunlight' and have definitive ties with the sun in several mythologies? Why are some Yava pointless, and others debilitating?)<br /> <b>PS: forcably dump the 'eyes of Gaia' thing. It's so obviously untrue of most of the Bastet Tribes that it seems pretty weird to have Silent Striders thinking that's the role of the Simba, or Shadow Lords claiming that to be the role of the Kahn, or either of them agreeing with it.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Kitsune Breedbook</b><br /> While they are currently Asia only, other than a few strays, they could easily be spread out. I don't think Luna created them to hide in a corner while the world goes to crap.<br /> <br /> <b>WoD: Sorcerer</b><br /> While Sorcerer Revised did a fair job on collecting most Numina under one banner, even at the time it was showing signs of being a little rushed. In this case, there's a whole thread of talk back and forth, and has been mentioned before in this thread. Knock it back out of the Mage banner, there's too much potential in it elsewhere, and really not as much under Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T09:03:07-07:00","id":1081452,"title":"","content":"Mage The Ascension: The War for Horizon.<br /> a module with details of how the horizon war took place while everything went AWOL.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T02:28:00-07:00","id":1082197,"title":"","content":"An armory/combat book. Detailing differences between hollow points and regular bullets for example or how damage a broken bottle does.<br /> <br /> Also, i would like to see 5th edition running a tighter ship, where you have the core gameline with stuff like general rules and for example the armory book mentioned above. Something all gamelines can benefit from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T18:54:28-07:00","id":1082478,"title":"","content":"I want a WOD 20 book which includes all the small splat books like bestial bygones and midnight carnival and all the rest of the book that never had a core splat book to attach too.<br /> <br /> Prehistory books for mage/vampire/changeling/demon/wraith/hunter - a book that gives you the rules to play as someone from the beginning of time or at least as close as the writers can get too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":3293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","user":"Rahod","date":". 04-22-2017, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T13:23:05-07:00","id":1082753,"title":"","content":"For C20 I'd like to see books covering Continental Europe and Mexico as well as more of North America. I'd like a big book covering the Native American Fay, not just the tribes from the Players Guide, but also the kith from <b>Kingdom of Willows</b>, Mexican Fay (Rain Dancers would be nice), and fix the Menehune (for starters they should all be invisible and they need a system for taboos).<br /> <br /> For M20 I'd like to see works like <b>Tales of Magick: Dark Adventure</b> but covering sets of Genres. Example: The first book could cover, Noir, Action, Urban Fantasy, and Twenty-Minuets-into-the-Future Sci Fi. The second book could cover Space Opera, Planetary Romance, Time Travel, and High Fantasy. Each book would do about sixty pages on each on a related set of genres with the last 15 pages being a worked out setting.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see splatbooks on the Disparates and the Five Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> For W20 those Guilds not covered in the original Wraith. Chantures especially.<br /> <br /> For Were20 give me some worked out Cearns described as playable settings and modles for making by own Caerns. Think about the books on Freeholds and Chantries.<br /> <br /> For all these lines I'll take a Sci Fi setting each, Reprints and extra details on the historical settings, and books covering setting up a master level PC (think of the books on Elder Vamps, give us the 10/7/5 level as opposed to the starter 7/5/3 level)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T14:28:33-07:00","id":1082769,"title":"","content":"I'd like a M20/C20 crossover of some sort. Possibly have it double as an \u201curban fantasy\u201d genre book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:07:11-07:00","id":1082782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1042199#post1042199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W:TA - Mockery Breeds: Focuses on the mockery breeds created by Pentex and its minions. Along with the chance of at least one of them joining Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd pay good money for this. I absolutely love the Mockery Breeds.<br /> Other than that, I want a <i>good</i> Sorcery book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T03:34:22-07:00","id":1083396,"title":"","content":"C20: The Shattering - Part guide, part adventure that leads from DA: Fae, through the Shattering, and into the Interregnum. In theory, you'd be able to play a faerie soul through various incarnations, but get the pleasure of creating new characters at the same time.<br /> <br /> Wr20: Guildbooks - Finishing the series.<br /> <br /> V20 Clanbook: Baali - The original DA book on the Baali was one of my favourites. I'd love a modern take on the bloodline, exploring their connections to the Assamites, Salubri and Lasombra, as well as the rich pantheon of gods and demons they worship/serve/placate. The Children were mostly forgotten about after the first Clanbook, and I think that's a shame. They were sort-of-Malfean, sort-of-Antediluvian, sort-of-Earthbound, but more interesting than any one of those answers alone. When their infernal masters 'just' because Earthbound, it was far less interesting. Alternatively, you could expand this into an infernal sourcebook for vampires in general. Call it Twice Damned or Double Damned: The Infernalist's Handbook, for instance.<br /> <br /> Immortals - An update on the non-MTR mummies from across cultures. You could throw in non-Asian Wan Kuei analogues too. It strikes me as unlikely that the Cabiri etc would renew their own Spell of Life like the Amenti did. There also the old-school mummies who refused the new Spell of Life--what are they up to now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T21:03:04-07:00","id":1134738,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the rest of the Wraith guilds getting their own books as well. With pre and post Ends of the Empire options so you can use it in either setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 08-28-2017, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T14:56:53-07:00","id":1146168,"title":"","content":"A book that updates what's been going on in the By Night cities. I'm sure things have gotten pretty testy in Atlanta (Necropolis Atlanta) with BLM and the anti-Trump and race riots there. (The Sons of the Imperial Dragon must be having a field day.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T01:40:18-07:00","id":1146279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1080930#post1080930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage: TA<br /> -Guide to the Disparate Alliance (Come on, they need it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nephandi also need a Guide to them, and they were here first.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1083396#post1083396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 Clanbook: Baali - The original DA book on the Baali was one of my favourites. I'd love a modern take on the bloodline, exploring their connections to the Assamites, Salubri and Lasombra, as well as the rich pantheon of gods and demons they worship/serve/placate</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the Baali are very much in need of a Clanbook.<br /> Could they be called a Clan? They seem far more active and important than the Giovanni in many events concerning the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-03-2017, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T14:32:50-07:00","id":1146446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1146279#post1146279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nephandi also need a Guide to them, and they were here first.</div> </div> </div> </div>At most, you might need a section in a book about antagonists. All of the Shadow-archetype characters (Sabbat, BSDs, etc.) basically boil down to being nihilistic, self-centered douchebags who are so apathetic that they messed themselves up thinking that they already knew the worst of experiences, and now spend all of their time trying to convince themselves that it was somehow a deep or meaningful statement about the world, the &quot;real deal&quot; of existence, etc., when in fact they have just messed themselves up and think that everyone else should be messed up that way, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T08:10:17-07:00","id":1146669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1146279#post1146279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nephandi also need a Guide to them, and they were here first..</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nephandi are covered in both versions of the Book of Madness with plenty of rules and ideas how to play them.<br /> <br /> There should totally be a setting for ancient Rome. We could call it &quot;Age of Rome&quot; and it could cover...<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b>: The glory age for Vampires, we get to see Carthridge (maybe even save it) and what was it like for the Salubri when they were a full clan.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b>: While the White Howlers finally got a Tribebook, it would be great to see a time before the Black Spiral Dancers and what the Wyrm did to compensate that.<br /> <br /> <b>Wraith</b>: Live in the early days of the Strygia when the Deathlords were a senate,<br /> <br /> <b>EXTRAS</b>: Fall of Rome sourcebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 10-04-2017, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T09:14:09-07:00","id":1146694,"title":"","content":"I'd really love to see Becket's Jyhad Diary style metaplot books for W20 and M20","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T17:46:34-07:00","id":1147621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1082197#post1082197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An armory/combat book. Detailing differences between hollow points and regular bullets for example or how damage a broken bottle does.<br /> <br /> Also, i would like to see 5th edition running a tighter ship, where you have the core gameline with stuff like general rules and for example the armory book mentioned above. Something all gamelines can benefit from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what NWoD/CoD did?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T17:54:38-07:00","id":1147623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1146446#post1146446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At most, you might need a section in a book about antagonists. All of the Shadow-archetype characters (Sabbat, BSDs, etc.) basically boil down to being nihilistic, self-centered douchebags who are so apathetic that they messed themselves up thinking that they already knew the worst of experiences, and now spend all of their time trying to convince themselves that it was somehow a deep or meaningful statement about the world, the &quot;real deal&quot; of existence, etc., when in fact they have just messed themselves up and think that everyone else should be messed up that way, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of the Nephandi, aren't those that have been through the Caul essentially puppets of the inhuman entities they serve? Or am I misremembering?<br /> <br /> After Wraith: The Great War came out back in the day, I was disappointed that there was never a book entirely about Mortwights that flipped Wraith on its head and was about dying and being reborn as a Spectre and trying to crawl your way away from Oblivion and become a normal wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T00:56:15-07:00","id":1147701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1147623#post1147623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After Wraith: The Great War came out back in the day, I was disappointed that there was never a book entirely about Mortwights that flipped Wraith on its head and was about dying and being reborn as a Spectre and trying to crawl your way away from Oblivion and become a normal wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div> You mean like <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dark_Reflections:_Spectres\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Reflections: Spectres</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T07:24:10-07:00","id":1147754,"title":"","content":"Still holding out hope for a WoD:Sorcerer 20, collecting most things from the various Hunter and Ally books and cleaning them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T12:30:22-07:00","id":1147851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1147701#post1147701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You mean like <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dark_Reflections:_Spectres\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Reflections: Spectres</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I own that, and a lot of the original Black Dog books were really more about shock value or just generic &quot;playing the bad guy&quot; without really going into what that meant with any depth or detail. I'm talking about a book that is almost entirely &quot;I am a monster born of catastrophic physical and emotional trauma used as a tool for nihilism, but deep in the core of my soul, I struggle for something more and am going to attempt the long hard climb out of hell to reach it.&quot; But I've always seen Wraith as, at it's heart, being a game about getting a second chance after you die, and I think such a book would've been in tune with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T13:36:39-07:00","id":1194962,"title":"","content":"<b>Drowned Blood: </b>Beckett's Jyhad Diary revealed that South America has some hidden Bloodlines (the Drowned Legacies) that have finally made themselves known and are taking South America by storm. Much like Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, the book will focus on these mysterious Vampires and South America. (Our very own Crowly once joked to me that Chile is pretty much Sabbat territory.) The famine crisis in Venezuela alone must be hard for the Vampires in that area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T03:02:33-07:00","id":1195668,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I do hope that we'd eventually get Demon 20th anniversary. There were things in demon I'd like to see spun and worked on again after years of letting the whole satanism and rpgs thing die down. I never got to play demon, but I always wanted to, but there were many weird little things that made it hard to play and sell. <br /> <br /> Though since demon was last of original WW line and not in the top sellers, I have no idea if it'd ever come to pass. Still, wishlist is wishlist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12705-xararion","name":"Xararion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T07:15:41-07:00","id":1195718,"title":"","content":"I'm not expecting but HOPING for a Hunter the Reckoning 20th announcement soon. If not, hey, it's not expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T04:35:24-07:00","id":1196009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363273-what-kind-of-books-would-you-like-in-the-future?p=1195718#post1195718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not expecting but HOPING for a Hunter the Reckoning 20th announcement soon. If not, hey, it's not expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure about soon.<br /> <br /> Going by the 20 in '20th', the timeline would be as follows;<br /> <br /> 2018 - Kindred Of The East<br /> 2019 - Hunter: The Reckoning<br /> 2021 - Mummy: The resurrection<br /> 2022 - Demon: The fallen<br /> <br /> (neglecting any actual time it takes to make the books, of course..)<br /> <br /> Either way, KoTE *should* be next in line, and I think the chances for that just quadrupled by the recent inclusion of KoTE into the StoryTeller Vault <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statist